"tags":[],"url":"/concepts/agents#setting-one-up","content":"Setting one up"},"7":{"id":"/concepts/agents-5","page_id":"/concepts/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/agents","content":"An **agent** is a spender that is a program rather than a person. It is added to the team account like any other spender, with two differences: it signs with its own Stellar key, and its payments that break a rule are refused instead of held."},"8":{"id":"/concepts/agents-6","page_id":"/concepts/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/agents#what-an-agent-can-do","content":"**Pay on a schedule.** For example, `$5 every day` to a `market-data` service."},"9":{"id":"/concepts/agents-7","page_id":"/concepts/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/agents#what-an-agent-can-do","content":"Every payment goes through the full contract check order. The agent's policy decides how much, how often, until when and to which services."},"10":{"id":"/concepts/agents-8","page_id":"/concepts/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/agents#its-own-key","content":"Each agent gets its own Stellar key. That key is only useful as that spender: it cannot withdraw, change policies, approve requests or pay services outside its list. If the key leaks, the most it can do is what the agent's policy already allows, and the owner can pause or remove the agent at once."},"11":{"id":"/concepts/agents-9","page_id":"/concepts/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/agents#refused-means-refused","content":"A person who hits a limit can ask for approval. An agent cannot: its policy's `kind` is `Agent`, and the contract answers `request_approval` with `AgentCannotRequest`. Its refused payments end with a refused receipt and nothing moves. This keeps an agent from filling the owner's Approvals screen, and it makes the policy the single place where an agent's room to spend is decided."},"12":{"id":"/concepts/agents-10","page_id":"/concepts/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/agents#setting-one-up","content":"Generate a Stellar key for the agent where it will run. The web app never holds it."},"13":{"id":"/concepts/agents-11","page_id":"/concepts/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/agents#setting-one-up","content":"On **Spenders**, add the agent's address as an *AI agent* with a tight policy: a small cap, a low allowance, a short expiry and only the services it needs."},"14":{"id":"/concepts/agents-12","page_id":"/concepts/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/agents#setting-one-up","content":"On **Agents**, record its schedule (amount, service, every hour/day/week) so the team can see what it is meant to do."},"15":{"id":"/concepts/agents-13","page_id":"/concepts/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/agents#setting-one-up","content":"Run the agent worker with its key:"},"16":{"id":"/concepts/agents-14","page_id":"/concepts/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/agents#setting-one-up","content":"The worker records each payment's idempotency key before submitting. After a crash it asks the contract whether that key was used (`is_key_used`) rather than paying again."},"17":{"id":"/concepts/agents-15","page_id":"/concepts/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/agents#setting-one-up","content":"Watch its receipts in **Activity**."},"18":{"id":"/concepts/agents-16","page_id":"/concepts/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/agents#setting-one-up","content":"In the sandbox, the browser tab plays the worker: schedules run on their own, and **Run now** runs one immediately."},"19":{"id":"/concepts/agents-17","page_id":"/concepts/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/agents#setting-one-up","content":"Suggested starting point for a data-feed agent: cap `$5`, allowance `$150 / month`, max payments `31 / month`, one approved service."},"20":{"id":"/concepts/approvals","page_id":"/concepts/approvals","type":"page","content":"Approvals","breadcrumbs":["EcoRouter Docs","Concepts"],"tags":[],"url":"/concepts/approvals"},"21":{"id":"/concepts/approvals-0","page_id":"/concepts/approvals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/approvals","content":"Over a limit, a payment is held, not failed, and the owner decides."},"22":{"id":"/concepts/approvals-1","page_id":"/concepts/approvals","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/approvals#the-flow","content":"The flow"},"23":{"id":"/concepts/approvals-2","page_id":"/concepts/approvals","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/approvals#what-cannot-be-approved","content":"What cannot be approved"},"24":{"id":"/concepts/approvals-3","page_id":"/concepts/approvals","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/approvals#agents-do-not-ask","content":"Agents do not ask"},"25":{"id":"/concepts/approvals-4","page_id":"/concepts/approvals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/approvals","content":"When a person's payment breaks one of four rules, it is **held**: the service is not on their approved list, the amount is over the cap per payment, they have used up their payments for the period, or the amount is over the allowance left. Nothing moves. The payment is not lost either: the spender can ask the owner for an exception to that one payment."},"26":{"id":"/concepts/approvals-5","page_id":"/concepts/approvals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/approvals#the-flow","content":"**Held.** The spender sees which rule caught the payment and how far over it was, for example `per-payment cap $250 · over by $70`."},"27":{"id":"/concepts/approvals-6","page_id":"/concepts/approvals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/approvals#the-flow","content":"**Ask for approval.** The spender files a request (`request_approval`). It lands on the owner's **Approvals** screen with the spender, service, amount, memo, the rule that caught it and the overage. The contract also records the service's payee at that moment. Requests expire after 7 days."},"28":{"id":"/concepts/approvals-7","page_id":"/concepts/approvals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/approvals#the-flow","content":"**Approve or decline.** The owner decides. Declining closes the request and writes a declined receipt."},"29":{"id":"/concepts/approvals-8","page_id":"/concepts/approvals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/approvals#the-flow","content":"**Settle.** Approving does not move money. Settlement (`settle`) is its own transaction, sent by the owner or by the spender who asked. It refuses if the service's payee changed since the request was filed, and also if the account is paused, the request expired, the service is now unknown or suspended, or the balance is too low. A settled exception does not count against the spender's allowance."},"30":{"id":"/concepts/approvals-9","page_id":"/concepts/approvals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/approvals#the-flow","content":"Keeping approval and settlement separate means an approval is a decision about one specific payment to one specific payee, not a blank cheque."},"31":{"id":"/concepts/approvals-10","page_id":"/concepts/approvals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/approvals#what-cannot-be-approved","content":"Some checks cannot be overridden by an approval:"},"32":{"id":"/concepts/approvals-11","page_id":"/concepts/approvals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/approvals#what-cannot-be-approved","content":"the account or the spender is paused,"},"33":{"id":"/concepts/approvals-12","page_id":"/concepts/approvals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/approvals#what-cannot-be-approved","content":"the caller is not a spender, or the policy has expired,"},"34":{"id":"/concepts/approvals-13","page_id":"/concepts/approvals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/approvals#what-cannot-be-approved","content":"the amount is zero or negative,"},"35":{"id":"/concepts/approvals-14","page_id":"/concepts/approvals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/approvals#what-cannot-be-approved","content":"the replay key was already used,"},"36":{"id":"/concepts/approvals-15","page_id":"/concepts/approvals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/approvals#what-cannot-be-approved","content":"the service is unknown or suspended in the registry,"},"37":{"id":"/concepts/approvals-16","page_id":"/concepts/approvals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/approvals#what-cannot-be-approved","content":"the account does not hold enough USDC."},"38":{"id":"/concepts/approvals-17","page_id":"/concepts/approvals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/approvals#what-cannot-be-approved","content":"These are **refused** outright. Even a request for a service outside the spender's list must name a service the registry resolves; payments never go to a raw address."},"39":{"id":"/concepts/approvals-18","page_id":"/concepts/approvals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/approvals#agents-do-not-ask","content":"An agent's payment that breaks a limit is refused and stops there. It does not create an approval request. If an agent needs more room, the owner changes its policy. See Agents."},"40":{"id":"/concepts/assistant","page_id":"/concepts/assistant","type":"page","content":"Assistant","breadcrumbs":["EcoRouter Docs","Concepts"],"tags":[],"url":"/concepts/assistant"},"41":{"id":"/concepts/assistant-0","page_id":"/concepts/assistant","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/assistant","content":"Ask for a payment in plain words. Five stages check it, and any one can refuse."},"42":{"id":"/concepts/assistant-1","page_id":"/concepts/assistant","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/assistant#the-five-stages","content":"The five stages"},"43":{"id":"/concepts/assistant-2","page_id":"/concepts/assistant","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/assistant#why-a-hallucinated-recipient-cannot-happen","content":"Why a hallucinated recipient cannot happen"},"44":{"id":"/concepts/assistant-3","page_id":"/concepts/assistant","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/assistant#why-the-amount-comes-from-code","content":"Why the amount comes from code"},"45":{"id":"/concepts/assistant-4","page_id":"/concepts/assistant","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/assistant#what-the-assistant-cannot-do","content":"What the assistant cannot do"},"46":{"id":"/concepts/assistant-5","page_id":"/concepts/assistant","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/assistant","content":"The **assistant** lets a spender type a sentence such as `top up our inference credits by $120` instead of filling in the payment form. What it produces is a **proposal**. It has no power to pay; the contract still decides."},"47":{"id":"/concepts/assistant-6","page_id":"/concepts/assistant","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/assistant#the-five-stages","content":"| Stage       | What happens                                         | Refuses when                                           |\n| ----------- | ---------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| 1. Sentence | Code, not the model, reads the amount from the text. | There is no amount, or more than one different amount. |","table":"table-0"},"48":{"id":"/concepts/assistant-7","page_id":"/concepts/assistant","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/assistant#the-five-stages","content":"| Stage        | What happens                                                          | Refuses when                          |\n| ------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| 2. Assistant | The model picks a service, but only from the spender's approved list. | No approved service fits the request. |","table":"table-0"},"49":{"id":"/concepts/assistant-8","page_id":"/concepts/assistant","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/assistant#the-five-stages","content":"| Stage     | What happens                                                      | Refuses when                         |\n| --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| 3. Schema | The output must match a fixed shape: `{ service, amount, memo }`. | The output does not match the shape. |","table":"table-0"},"50":{"id":"/concepts/assistant-9","page_id":"/concepts/assistant","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/assistant#the-five-stages","content":"| Stage       | What happens                                          | Refuses when                    |\n| ----------- | ----------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| 4. Registry | The service id must resolve in the on-chain registry. | The id is unknown or suspended. |","table":"table-0"},"51":{"id":"/concepts/assistant-10","page_id":"/concepts/assistant","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/assistant#the-five-stages","content":"| Stage     | What happens                   | Refuses when                                                             |\n| --------- | ------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| 5. Policy | The full contract policy runs. | A rule fails. A person's limit becomes a hold; anything else is refused. |","table":"table-0"},"52":{"id":"/concepts/assistant-11","page_id":"/concepts/assistant","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/assistant#why-a-hallucinated-recipient-cannot-happen","content":"The assistant's output shape has **no address field**. The only way to name a destination is a service id, and the only ids it may choose are on the spender's list. An invented address has nowhere to go, and an invented id fails at the registry."},"53":{"id":"/concepts/assistant-12","page_id":"/concepts/assistant","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/assistant#why-the-amount-comes-from-code","content":"Amounts are read from the sentence by deterministic code and compared with what the model returns. The model cannot change the amount you typed. If the sentence is ambiguous, the request stops at stage 1 and asks you to be specific."},"54":{"id":"/concepts/assistant-13","page_id":"/concepts/assistant","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/assistant#what-the-assistant-cannot-do","content":"It cannot add services to a list, raise a cap, approve a request or pay an address. Those are owner actions or do not exist at all."},"55":{"id":"/concepts/receipts","page_id":"/concepts/receipts","type":"page","content":"Receipts","breadcrumbs":["EcoRouter Docs","Concepts"],"tags":[],"url":"/concepts/receipts"},"56":{"id":"/concepts/receipts-0","page_id":"/concepts/receipts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/receipts","content":"Every payment attempt leaves a receipt in Activity."},"57":{"id":"/concepts/receipts-1","page_id":"/concepts/receipts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/receipts#outcomes","content":"Outcomes"},"58":{"id":"/concepts/receipts-2","page_id":"/concepts/receipts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/receipts#on-chain","content":"On chain"},"59":{"id":"/concepts/receipts-3","page_id":"/concepts/receipts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/receipts","content":"The **Activity** screen lists every payment attempt as a receipt. A receipt records who paid (the spender), the service id, the amount, the memo, the time, and the outcome."},"60":{"id":"/concepts/receipts-4","page_id":"/concepts/receipts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/receipts#outcomes","content":"| Outcome     | Meaning                                                  | Money moved |\n| ----------- | -------------------------------------------------------- | ----------- |\n| **Settled** | Every check passed and USDC went to the service's payee. | Yes         |","table":"table-0"},"61":{"id":"/concepts/receipts-5","page_id":"/concepts/receipts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/receipts#outcomes","content":"| Outcome  | Meaning                                                        | Money moved |\n| -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------- |\n| **Held** | A limit caught the payment. It may become an approval request. | No          |","table":"table-0"},"62":{"id":"/concepts/receipts-6","page_id":"/concepts/receipts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/receipts#outcomes","content":"| Outcome      | Meaning                                 | Money moved |\n| ------------ | --------------------------------------- | ----------- |\n| **Declined** | The owner declined an approval request. | No          |","table":"table-0"},"63":{"id":"/concepts/receipts-7","page_id":"/concepts/receipts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/receipts#outcomes","content":"| Outcome     | Meaning                                                          | Money moved |\n| ----------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------- |\n| **Refused** | A check that cannot be approved failed, or an agent hit a limit. | No          |","table":"table-0"},"64":{"id":"/concepts/receipts-8","page_id":"/concepts/receipts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/receipts#outcomes","content":"Held, declined and refused receipts carry the rule that stopped the payment and, for limits, how far over it was."},"65":{"id":"/concepts/receipts-9","page_id":"/concepts/receipts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/receipts#on-chain","content":"On Stellar testnet, a settled payment emits a `pay` event from the `team-account` contract carrying the spender, service, payee, amount, memo and the spender's spend this period. Settled exceptions emit a `request settled` event. The receipt in the app links to the Stellar transaction so anyone can check it. The replay key passed to `pay` means the same payment cannot be settled twice, even if the app retries."},"66":{"id":"/concepts/receipts-10","page_id":"/concepts/receipts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/receipts#on-chain","content":"A payment that fails a check never reaches the chain as a transfer, so held, declined and refused receipts are kept by the app; requests and decisions are also recorded as contract events."},"67":{"id":"/concepts/receipts-11","page_id":"/concepts/receipts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/receipts#on-chain","content":"In the sandbox, receipts are kept in your browser."},"68":{"id":"/concepts/services","page_id":"/concepts/services","type":"page","content":"Service registry","breadcrumbs":["EcoRouter Docs","Concepts"],"tags":[],"url":"/concepts/services"},"69":{"id":"/concepts/services-0","page_id":"/concepts/services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/services","content":"Payments go to registered services, named by id, never to a raw address."},"70":{"id":"/concepts/services-1","page_id":"/concepts/services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/services#why-payments-take-an-id-not-an-address","content":"Why payments take an id, not an address"},"71":{"id":"/concepts/services-2","page_id":"/concepts/services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/services#what-can-happen-to-a-service","content":"What can happen to a service"},"72":{"id":"/concepts/services-3","page_id":"/concepts/services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/services#who-controls-what","content":"Who controls what"},"73":{"id":"/concepts/services-4","page_id":"/concepts/services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/services#services-and-spenders","content":"Services and spenders"},"74":{"id":"/concepts/services-5","page_id":"/concepts/services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/services","content":"The **service registry** is a separate contract, `service-registry`, that maps a service id such as `inference-credits` to the Stellar address that receives payment for it (the **payee**)."},"75":{"id":"/concepts/services-6","page_id":"/concepts/services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/services#why-payments-take-an-id-not-an-address","content":"The team account's `pay` function takes a service id. It has no parameter for a destination address. At the end of its checks the contract asks the registry to resolve the id, and pays whatever address the registry returns."},"76":{"id":"/concepts/services-7","page_id":"/concepts/services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/services#why-payments-take-an-id-not-an-address","content":"This removes a whole class of mistakes and attacks: a mistyped address, a pasted address from a phishing message, or an address invented by a language model cannot be expressed as a payment."},"77":{"id":"/concepts/services-8","page_id":"/concepts/services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/services#what-can-happen-to-a-service","content":"| State              | Effect on payment                           |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------- |\n| Registered, active | Resolves to its payee. Payment can proceed. |","table":"table-0"},"78":{"id":"/concepts/services-9","page_id":"/concepts/services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/services#what-can-happen-to-a-service","content":"| State      | Effect on payment                         |\n| ---------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| Unknown id | Resolution fails and the payment reverts. |","table":"table-0"},"79":{"id":"/concepts/services-10","page_id":"/concepts/services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/services#what-can-happen-to-a-service","content":"| State     | Effect on payment                                                      |\n| --------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Suspended | Resolution fails and the payment reverts until the service is resumed. |","table":"table-0"},"80":{"id":"/concepts/services-11","page_id":"/concepts/services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/services#who-controls-what","content":"The **registry owner** registers services and can **suspend** or **resume** them. Service ids are never reused."},"81":{"id":"/concepts/services-12","page_id":"/concepts/services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/services#who-controls-what","content":"A service's **payee** can **rotate its payout address**, for example to move to a new wallet."},"82":{"id":"/concepts/services-13","page_id":"/concepts/services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/services#who-controls-what","content":"Because the payee can change, an approved exception records the payee at the time of the request, and settlement refuses if the payee has changed since. The owner then has to look at the request again."},"83":{"id":"/concepts/services-14","page_id":"/concepts/services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/services#services-and-spenders","content":"A spender's policy lists the service ids it may pay. The contract checks the allowlist before it checks the registry, so a payment to a registered service that is not on a spender's list fails for that spender. A person can ask the owner for a one-off approval; an agent cannot."},"84":{"id":"/concepts/services-15","page_id":"/concepts/services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/services#services-and-spenders","content":"See Contracts reference for the functions."},"85":{"id":"/concepts/spenders","page_id":"/concepts/spenders","type":"page","content":"Spenders and policies","breadcrumbs":["EcoRouter Docs","Concepts"],"tags":[],"url":"/concepts/spenders"},"86":{"id":"/concepts/spenders-0","page_id":"/concepts/spenders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/spenders","content":"Every person and every agent pays under its own on-chain policy."},"87":{"id":"/concepts/spenders-1","page_id":"/concepts/spenders","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/spenders#what-a-policy-holds","content":"What a policy holds"},"88":{"id":"/concepts/spenders-2","page_id":"/concepts/spenders","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/spenders#the-arithmetic","content":"The arithmetic"},"89":{"id":"/concepts/spenders-3","page_id":"/concepts/spenders","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/spenders#managing-spenders","content":"Managing spenders"},"90":{"id":"/concepts/spenders-4","page_id":"/concepts/spenders","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/spenders#people-and-agents","content":"People and agents"},"91":{"id":"/concepts/spenders-5","page_id":"/concepts/spenders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/spenders","content":"A **spender** is a Stellar address that may pay from the team account: a teammate's wallet or an AI agent's key. Each spender has exactly one **policy**, set by the owner."},"92":{"id":"/concepts/spenders-6","page_id":"/concepts/spenders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/spenders#what-a-policy-holds","content":"| Rule | Field  | Example         | What it does                     |\n| ---- | ------ | --------------- | -------------------------------- |\n| Kind | `kind` | Person or Agent | Agents cannot ask for approvals. |","table":"table-0"},"93":{"id":"/concepts/spenders-7","page_id":"/concepts/spenders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/spenders#what-a-policy-holds","content":"| Rule  | Field   | Example | What it does    |\n| ----- | ------- | ------- | --------------- |\n| Label | `label` | \"Sam\"   | A display name. |","table":"table-0"},"94":{"id":"/concepts/spenders-8","page_id":"/concepts/spenders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/spenders#what-a-policy-holds","content":"| Rule                 | Field       | Example | What it does                             |\n| -------------------- | ----------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| Allowance per period | `allowance` | $1,000  | Total the spender may pay in one period. |","table":"table-0"},"95":{"id":"/concepts/spenders-9","page_id":"/concepts/spenders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/spenders#what-a-policy-holds","content":"| Rule   | Field    | Example | What it does                                                                           |\n| ------ | -------- | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Period | `period` | 30 days | Length of a period. Periods are fixed windows counted from when the spender was added. |","table":"table-0"},"96":{"id":"/concepts/spenders-10","page_id":"/concepts/spenders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/spenders#what-a-policy-holds","content":"| Rule            | Field         | Example | What it does                                                    |\n| --------------- | ------------- | ------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Cap per payment | `max_payment` | $250    | No single payment may be larger. Must not exceed the allowance. |","table":"table-0"},"97":{"id":"/concepts/spenders-11","page_id":"/concepts/spenders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/spenders#what-a-policy-holds","content":"| Rule                    | Field          | Example | What it does                                          |\n| ----------------------- | -------------- | ------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| Max payments per period | `max_payments` | 20      | How many payments the spender may make in one period. |","table":"table-0"},"98":{"id":"/concepts/spenders-12","page_id":"/concepts/spenders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/spenders#what-a-policy-holds","content":"| Rule   | Field        | Example    | What it does                                            |\n| ------ | ------------ | ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Expiry | `expires_at` | 2026-12-31 | After this time, the policy stops authorizing anything. |","table":"table-0"},"99":{"id":"/concepts/spenders-13","page_id":"/concepts/spenders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/spenders#what-a-policy-holds","content":"| Rule              | Field      | Example                           | What it does                                          |\n| ----------------- | ---------- | --------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| Approved services | `services` | `inference-credits`, `gpu-rental` | The only service ids this spender may pay (up to 32). |","table":"table-0"},"100":{"id":"/concepts/spenders-14","page_id":"/concepts/spenders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/spenders#what-a-policy-holds","content":"| Rule   | Field    | Example | What it does                              |\n| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| Paused | `paused` | false   | When true, the spender cannot pay at all. |","table":"table-0"},"101":{"id":"/concepts/spenders-15","page_id":"/concepts/spenders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/spenders#what-a-policy-holds","content":"Every limit must be positive. A zero never means \"no limit\"."},"102":{"id":"/concepts/spenders-16","page_id":"/concepts/spenders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/spenders#what-a-policy-holds","content":"A policy only ever narrows what a spender can do. There is no rule that lets a spender pay an address directly, and no rule that lets one spender use another's allowance."},"103":{"id":"/concepts/spenders-17","page_id":"/concepts/spenders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/spenders#the-arithmetic","content":"The app shows the same arithmetic the contract runs. For a spender with an allowance of $900, $340 already spent and a cap of $250:"},"104":{"id":"/concepts/spenders-18","page_id":"/concepts/spenders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/spenders#managing-spenders","content":"**Add** a spender with an address and a policy."},"105":{"id":"/concepts/spenders-19","page_id":"/concepts/spenders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/spenders#managing-spenders","content":"**Edit** the policy at any time. Changes apply to the next payment; the current period and its usage are kept."},"106":{"id":"/concepts/spenders-20","page_id":"/concepts/spenders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/spenders#managing-spenders","content":"**Pause** a spender to stop them immediately without losing their history. **Resume** to undo."},"107":{"id":"/concepts/spenders-21","page_id":"/concepts/spenders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/spenders#managing-spenders","content":"**Remove** a spender to delete their policy. Their address can no longer pay; past receipts stay."},"108":{"id":"/concepts/spenders-22","page_id":"/concepts/spenders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/spenders#people-and-agents","content":"Both are spenders and both go through the same checks. The difference is what happens after a payment breaks a limit: a person's payment is held and can become an approval request; an agent's payment is refused and stops there. The contract knows which is which from the policy's `kind`."},"109":{"id":"/concepts/team-account","page_id":"/concepts/team-account","type":"page","content":"Team account","breadcrumbs":["EcoRouter Docs","Concepts"],"tags":[],"url":"/concepts/team-account"},"110":{"id":"/concepts/team-account-0","page_id":"/concepts/team-account","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/team-account","content":"One shared USDC account, held by a Soroban contract, that every spender pays from."},"111":{"id":"/concepts/team-account-1","page_id":"/concepts/team-account","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/team-account#the-owner","content":"The owner"},"112":{"id":"/concepts/team-account-2","page_id":"/concepts/team-account","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/team-account#balance-and-spend","content":"Balance and spend"},"113":{"id":"/concepts/team-account-3","page_id":"/concepts/team-account","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/team-account#pausing-the-account","content":"Pausing the account"},"114":{"id":"/concepts/team-account-4","page_id":"/concepts/team-account","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/concepts/team-account#sandbox-vs-testnet","content":"Sandbox vs testnet"},"115":{"id":"/concepts/team-account-5","page_id":"/concepts/team-account","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/team-account","content":"A team account is one instance of the `team-account` contract on Stellar. It holds the team's USDC and a policy for every spender. Nobody holds the money directly: not the owner's wallet, not a teammate, not an agent's key. Money leaves the account only through the contract's own functions, after its checks pass."},"116":{"id":"/concepts/team-account-6","page_id":"/concepts/team-account","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/team-account#the-owner","content":"Each team account has one **owner**, the address that created it. Only the owner can:"},"117":{"id":"/concepts/team-account-7","page_id":"/concepts/team-account","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/team-account#the-owner","content":"withdraw funds,"},"118":{"id":"/concepts/team-account-8","page_id":"/concepts/team-account","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/team-account#the-owner","content":"add, change, pause, resume and remove spenders,"},"119":{"id":"/concepts/team-account-9","page_id":"/concepts/team-account","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/team-account#the-owner","content":"pause and unpause the whole account,"},"120":{"id":"/concepts/team-account-10","page_id":"/concepts/team-account","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/team-account#the-owner","content":"approve or decline approval requests,"},"121":{"id":"/concepts/team-account-11","page_id":"/concepts/team-account","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/team-account#the-owner","content":"hand ownership to another address (a two-step propose and accept)."},"122":{"id":"/concepts/team-account-12","page_id":"/concepts/team-account","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/team-account#the-owner","content":"Anyone can fund the account: it is an ordinary USDC transfer to the contract's address. The app's **Deposit** action does exactly that."},"123":{"id":"/concepts/team-account-13","page_id":"/concepts/team-account","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/team-account#the-owner","content":"In the app, the owner sees the **Overview** (balance, spend this period, spenders) and the **Approvals** screen."},"124":{"id":"/concepts/team-account-14","page_id":"/concepts/team-account","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/team-account#balance-and-spend","content":"The balance is the USDC the contract holds. \"Spent this period\" is the sum of what spenders have paid inside their current periods. Each spender's allowance is tracked separately, so one spender running out never blocks another."},"125":{"id":"/concepts/team-account-15","page_id":"/concepts/team-account","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/team-account#balance-and-spend","content":"Amounts are USDC in 7-decimal integer units on chain. The app shows dollars and cents, and its pre-check uses the same integer arithmetic as the contract."},"126":{"id":"/concepts/team-account-16","page_id":"/concepts/team-account","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/team-account#pausing-the-account","content":"Pausing the account stops every payment from every spender at the first check, before anything else is looked at. It also blocks settlement of approved requests. Deposits and owner actions still work. Unpause to resume."},"127":{"id":"/concepts/team-account-17","page_id":"/concepts/team-account","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/team-account#sandbox-vs-testnet","content":"In the sandbox, the team account is a TypeScript object in your browser that mirrors the contract's rules and check order. On testnet, it is a deployed `team-account` contract and every change is a signed transaction."},"128":{"id":"/concepts/team-account-18","page_id":"/concepts/team-account","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/team-account#sandbox-vs-testnet","content":"See Contracts reference for the functions."},"129":{"id":"/contracts","page_id":"/contracts","type":"page","content":"Contracts reference","breadcrumbs":["EcoRouter Docs"],"tags":[],"url":"/contracts"},"130":{"id":"/contracts-0","page_id":"/contracts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/contracts","content":"Public functions, types, events and errors of the team-account and service-registry Soroban contracts."},"131":{"id":"/contracts-1","page_id":"/contracts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/contracts#team-account","content":"team-account"},"132":{"id":"/contracts-2","page_id":"/contracts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/contracts#construction","content":"Construction"},"133":{"id":"/contracts-3","page_id":"/contracts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/contracts#owner-functions","content":"Owner functions"},"134":{"id":"/contracts-4","page_id":"/contracts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/contracts#spender-functions","content":"Spender functions"},"135":{"id":"/contracts-5","page_id":"/contracts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/contracts#check-order-in-pay","content":"Check order in `pay`"},"136":{"id":"/contracts-6","page_id":"/contracts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/contracts#dry-run","content":"Dry run"},"137":{"id":"/contracts-7","page_id":"/contracts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/contracts#views","content":"Views"},"138":{"id":"/contracts-8","page_id":"/contracts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/contracts#types","content":"Types"},"139":{"id":"/contracts-9","page_id":"/contracts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/contracts#events","content":"Events"},"140":{"id":"/contracts-10","page_id":"/contracts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/contracts#errors","content":"Errors"},"141":{"id":"/contracts-11","page_id":"/contracts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/contracts#service-registry","content":"service-registry"},"142":{"id":"/contracts-12","page_id":"/contracts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/contracts#building","content":"Building"},"143":{"id":"/contracts-13","page_id":"/contracts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/contracts","content":"Two Soroban contracts make up EcoRouter on Stellar. Both live in the repository under `contracts/`."},"144":{"id":"/contracts-14","page_id":"/contracts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/contracts","content":"| Contract       | Path                     | Purpose                                                                       |\n| -------------- | ------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `team-account` | `contracts/team-account` | Holds the team's USDC, stores a policy per spender, runs the checks and pays. |","table":"table-0"},"145":{"id":"/contracts-15","page_id":"/contracts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/contracts","content":"| Contract           | Path                         | Purpose                                              |\n| ------------------ | ---------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `service-registry` | `contracts/service-registry` | Resolves a service id to the address that gets paid. |","table":"table-0"},"146":{"id":"/contracts-16","page_id":"/contracts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/contracts","content":"This page summarizes the public interface. The Rust source in `contracts/` is authoritative. Amounts are in the asset's atomic units (USDC has 7 decimals). Times are ledger timestamps in seconds."},"147":{"id":"/contracts-17","page_id":"/contracts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/contracts#construction","content":"`__constructor(owner, asset, registry)` sets the owner, the token contract to pay in (USDC) and the service registry. The account starts unpaused with no spenders."},"148":{"id":"/contracts-18","page_id":"/contracts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/contracts#construction","content":"There is no deposit function. To fund the account, transfer USDC to the contract's address; `balance()` reads the contract's token balance."},"149":{"id":"/contracts-19","page_id":"/contracts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/contracts#owner-functions","content":"All of these require the owner's signature."},"150":{"id":"/contracts-20","page_id":"/contracts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/contracts#owner-functions","content":"| Function                                  | Effect                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n| ----------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `set_policy(spender, input: PolicyInput)` | Creates a spender or fully replaces its policy. A new spender starts a fresh period; an existing one keeps its period, usage and pause state. Fails with `InvalidPolicy` if any limit is not positive, `max_payment > allowance`, `expires_at` is not in the future, or more than 32 services are listed. |","table":"table-1"},"151":{"id":"/contracts-21","page_id":"/contracts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/contracts#owner-functions","content":"| Function                              | Effect                         |\n| ------------------------------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| `set_spender_paused(spender, paused)` | Pauses or resumes one spender. |","table":"table-1"},"152":{"id":"/contracts-22","page_id":"/contracts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/contracts#owner-functions","content":"| Function                  | Effect                                  |\n| ------------------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `remove_spender(spender)` | Deletes the spender's policy and usage. |","table":"table-1"},"153":{"id":"/contracts-23","page_id":"/contracts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/contracts#owner-functions","content":"| Function             | Effect                                                                                                               |\n| -------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `set_paused(paused)` | Pauses or resumes the whole account. A paused account authorizes nothing, including settlement of approved requests. |","table":"table-1"},"154":{"id":"/contracts-24","page_id":"/contracts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/contracts#owner-functions","content":"| Function               | Effect                         |\n| ---------------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| `withdraw(to, amount)` | Moves USDC out of the account. |","table":"table-1"},"155":{"id":"/contracts-25","page_id":"/contracts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/contracts#owner-functions","content":"| Function      | Effect                                                 |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `approve(id)` | Approves a pending, unexpired request. Moves no money. |","table":"table-1"},"156":{"id":"/contracts-26","page_id":"/contracts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/contracts#owner-functions","content":"| Function      | Effect                                                |\n| ------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `decline(id)` | Declines a pending or approved-but-unsettled request. |","table":"table-1"},"157":{"id":"/contracts-27","page_id":"/contracts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/contracts#owner-functions","content":"| Function                   | Effect                                                                     |\n| -------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `propose_owner(new_owner)` | First step of an ownership transfer. The new owner calls `accept_owner()`. |","table":"table-1"},"158":{"id":"/contracts-28","page_id":"/contracts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/contracts#spender-functions","content":"| Function                                              | Auth    | Effect                                                                                                                                                                                                                           |\n| ----------------------------------------------------- | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `pay(spender, service, amount, memo, key) -> Receipt` | spender | Runs the checks below, transfers to the payee the registry returns, and emits a `pay` event. There is no recipient parameter. `key` is a 32-byte one-time key chosen by the caller, so a retried submission can never pay twice. |","table":"table-2"},"159":{"id":"/contracts-29","page_id":"/contracts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/contracts#spender-functions","content":"| Function                                                  | Auth    | Effect                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| --------------------------------------------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `request_approval(spender, service, amount, memo) -> u64` | spender | Files a request for a payment that one of the exception-eligible rules refused. People only. Records the rule, how far over it was, and the payee the registry returns now. Nothing moves. Requests expire after 7 days. |","table":"table-2"},"160":{"id":"/contracts-30","page_id":"/contracts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/contracts#spender-functions","content":"| Function             | Auth                              | Effect                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            |\n| -------------------- | --------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `settle(id, caller)` | owner or the spender who filed it | Pays an approved request. Refuses if the account is paused, the request is not approved or has expired, the service no longer resolves, **the payee changed since the request was filed** (`PayeeChanged`), or the balance is too low. Settled exceptions do not consume the spender's allowance. |","table":"table-2"},"161":{"id":"/contracts-31","page_id":"/contracts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/contracts#check-order-in-pay","content":"Account paused → `AccountPaused`"},"162":{"id":"/contracts-32","page_id":"/contracts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/contracts#check-order-in-pay","content":"Spender exists → `UnknownSpender`"},"163":{"id":"/contracts-33","page_id":"/contracts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/contracts#check-order-in-pay","content":"Spender paused → `SpenderPaused`"},"164":{"id":"/contracts-34","page_id":"/contracts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/contracts#check-order-in-pay","content":"Policy expired → `PolicyExpired`"},"165":{"id":"/contracts-35","page_id":"/contracts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/contracts#check-order-in-pay","content":"Amount > 0 → `InvalidAmount`"},"166":{"id":"/contracts-36","page_id":"/contracts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/contracts#check-order-in-pay","content":"Service on the spender's allowlist → `ServiceNotAllowed`"},"167":{"id":"/contracts-37","page_id":"/contracts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/contracts#check-order-in-pay","content":"Replay key unused → `DuplicatePayment`"},"168":{"id":"/contracts-38","page_id":"/contracts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/contracts#check-order-in-pay","content":"Per-payment cap (`max_payment`) → `OverPaymentCap`"},"169":{"id":"/contracts-39","page_id":"/contracts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/contracts#check-order-in-pay","content":"Payments per period (`max_payments`) → `OverFrequency`"},"170":{"id":"/contracts-40","page_id":"/contracts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/contracts#check-order-in-pay","content":"Allowance left this period → `OverAllowance`"},"171":{"id":"/contracts-41","page_id":"/contracts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/contracts#check-order-in-pay","content":"Registry resolves the service → `UnknownService`, `ServiceSuspended` or `RegistryUnavailable`"},"172":{"id":"/contracts-42","page_id":"/contracts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/contracts#check-order-in-pay","content":"Balance covers the amount → `InsufficientFunds`"},"173":{"id":"/contracts-43","page_id":"/contracts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/contracts#check-order-in-pay","content":"Transfer, then the `pay` receipt event"},"174":{"id":"/contracts-44","page_id":"/contracts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/contracts#check-order-in-pay","content":"Rules 6, 8, 9 and 10 are **exception-eligible**: a person whose payment fails one of them can call `request_approval`. Agents get `AgentCannotRequest`."},"175":{"id":"/contracts-45","page_id":"/contracts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/contracts#dry-run","content":"`check(spender, service, amount) -> Verdict` runs the same rules without auth or state changes an