---------------------------- |\n| `POLICY_EXCEEDED` | `PolicyExceededError` | Challenge amount exceeds `policy.maxSpendUsdc`. |","table":"table-0"},"245":{"id":"/legacy/api/errors-6","page_id":"/legacy/api/errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/errors","content":"| Code               | Class                  | Thrown when                                             |\n| ------------------ | ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `MANDATE_EXCEEDED` | `MandateExceededError` | Amount exceeds `maxPaymentAtomic` or `remainingAtomic`. |","table":"table-0"},"246":{"id":"/legacy/api/errors-7","page_id":"/legacy/api/errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/errors","content":"| Code              | Class                 | Thrown when                              |\n| ----------------- | --------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `MANDATE_EXPIRED` | `MandateExpiredError` | `mandate.expiresAt` is at or before now. |","table":"table-0"},"247":{"id":"/legacy/api/errors-8","page_id":"/legacy/api/errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/errors","content":"| Code              | Class                 | Thrown when             |\n| ----------------- | --------------------- | ----------------------- |\n| `MANDATE_REVOKED` | `MandateRevokedError` | The mandate is revoked. |","table":"table-0"},"248":{"id":"/legacy/api/errors-9","page_id":"/legacy/api/errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/errors","content":"| Code                          | Class                       | Thrown when                                                                  |\n| ----------------------------- | --------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `PAYMENT_AUTHORIZATION_ERROR` | `PaymentAuthorizationError` | Your `PaymentClient` threw it; signing or authorization definitively failed. |","table":"table-0"},"249":{"id":"/legacy/api/errors-10","page_id":"/legacy/api/errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/errors","content":"| Code                       | Class                    | Thrown when                                                      |\n| -------------------------- | ------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `PAYMENT_SETTLEMENT_ERROR` | `PaymentSettlementError` | Your `PaymentClient` threw it; the transfer definitively failed. |","table":"table-0"},"250":{"id":"/legacy/api/errors-11","page_id":"/legacy/api/errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/errors","content":"| Code                         | Class                           | Thrown when                                                              |\n| ---------------------------- | ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `PAYMENT_SETTLEMENT_UNKNOWN` | `PaymentSettlementUnknownError` | `authorizeAndSettle` threw anything else; settlement may have succeeded. |","table":"table-0"},"251":{"id":"/legacy/api/errors-12","page_id":"/legacy/api/errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/errors","content":"| Code                       | Class                    | Thrown when                                                    |\n| -------------------------- | ------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `PROVIDER_EXECUTION_ERROR` | `ProviderExecutionError` | The paid provider request failed (non-2xx or transport error). |","table":"table-0"},"252":{"id":"/legacy/api/errors-13","page_id":"/legacy/api/errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/errors","content":"| Code                      | Class                   | Thrown when                                                               |\n| ------------------------- | ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `PROVIDER_RESPONSE_ERROR` | `ProviderResponseError` | The paid response did not match `{ results: [{ title, url, snippet }] }`. |","table":"table-0"},"253":{"id":"/legacy/api/errors-14","page_id":"/legacy/api/errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/errors#paymentsettlementunknownerror","content":"Beyond `code` and `executionId`, it carries:"},"254":{"id":"/legacy/api/errors-15","page_id":"/legacy/api/errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/errors#paymentsettlementunknownerror","content":"<TypeTable type=\"{ providerId: { description: 'The winning provider the settlement targeted.', type: 'string' }, tran…\" />"},"255":{"id":"/legacy/api/errors-16","page_id":"/legacy/api/errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/errors#paymentsettlementunknownerror","content":"Executions that end `settlement_unknown` cannot be retried under the same `executionId`; the router throws instead of risking a double payment."},"256":{"id":"/legacy/api/payment-client","page_id":"/legacy/api/payment-client","type":"page","content":"Payment Client","breadcrumbs":["EcoRouter Docs","Legacy SDK","API Reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/legacy/api/payment-client"},"257":{"id":"/legacy/api/payment-client-0","page_id":"/legacy/api/payment-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/payment-client","content":"The PaymentClient interface you implement, its types, and its error contract."},"258":{"id":"/legacy/api/payment-client-1","page_id":"/legacy/api/payment-client","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/legacy/api/payment-client#paymentclient","content":"PaymentClient"},"259":{"id":"/legacy/api/payment-client-2","page_id":"/legacy/api/payment-client","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/legacy/api/payment-client#mandatestate","content":"MandateState"},"260":{"id":"/legacy/api/payment-client-3","page_id":"/legacy/api/payment-client","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/legacy/api/payment-client#signedpayment-and-settlementreceipt","content":"SignedPayment and SettlementReceipt"},"261":{"id":"/legacy/api/payment-client-4","page_id":"/legacy/api/payment-client","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/legacy/api/payment-client#error-contract","content":"Error contract"},"262":{"id":"/legacy/api/payment-client-5","page_id":"/legacy/api/payment-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/payment-client","content":"The SDK does not ship a Stellar transport implementation. You provide a `PaymentClient` that reads mandate state and submits the authorized transfer. The router treats its return value and its errors precisely."},"263":{"id":"/legacy/api/payment-client-6","page_id":"/legacy/api/payment-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/payment-client#paymentclient","content":"<TypeTable type=\"{ 'loadMandate(account)': { description: 'Read the current on-chain mandate for the account contract…\" />"},"264":{"id":"/legacy/api/payment-client-7","page_id":"/legacy/api/payment-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/payment-client#paymentclient","content":"`authorizeAndSettle` receives `{ account, sessionSecret, executionId, providerId, challenge }`."},"265":{"id":"/legacy/api/payment-client-8","page_id":"/legacy/api/payment-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/payment-client#mandatestate","content":"<TypeTable type=\"{ asset: { description: 'Asset identifier the mandate allows (USDC).', type: 'string', required: tru…\" />"},"266":{"id":"/legacy/api/payment-client-9","page_id":"/legacy/api/payment-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/payment-client#signedpayment-and-settlementreceipt","content":"`SignedPayment` is `{ payload: string; transactionHash?: string }`. The payload is sent back to the provider in the `payment-signature` header."},"267":{"id":"/legacy/api/payment-client-10","page_id":"/legacy/api/payment-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/payment-client#signedpayment-and-settlementreceipt","content":"`SettlementReceipt` is `{ transactionHash: string }`. The hash is returned in `result.payment.transactionHash`."},"268":{"id":"/legacy/api/payment-client-11","page_id":"/legacy/api/payment-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/payment-client#error-contract","content":"Throw the typed errors for definite failures:"},"269":{"id":"/legacy/api/payment-client-12","page_id":"/legacy/api/payment-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/payment-client#error-contract","content":"`PaymentAuthorizationError` when signing or authorization definitively failed."},"270":{"id":"/legacy/api/payment-client-13","page_id":"/legacy/api/payment-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/payment-client#error-contract","content":"`PaymentSettlementError` when the transfer definitively failed on-chain."},"271":{"id":"/legacy/api/payment-client-14","page_id":"/legacy/api/payment-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/payment-client#error-contract","content":"Both propagate unchanged and mark the execution `failed`, so the same `executionId` can be retried."},"272":{"id":"/legacy/api/payment-client-15","page_id":"/legacy/api/payment-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/payment-client#error-contract","content":"**Any other thrown value marks the execution `settlement_unknown`** and the router throws `PaymentSettlementUnknownError`, because the payment may have succeeded. A `settlement_unknown` execution id cannot be retried; retrying throws. Only throw a generic error when settlement truly is ambiguous."},"273":{"id":"/legacy/api/providers","page_id":"/legacy/api/providers","type":"page","content":"Providers","breadcrumbs":["EcoRouter Docs","Legacy SDK","API Reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/legacy/api/providers"},"274":{"id":"/legacy/api/providers-0","page_id":"/legacy/api/providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/providers","content":"The HTTP contract a web.search provider must implement."},"275":{"id":"/legacy/api/providers-1","page_id":"/legacy/api/providers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/legacy/api/providers#challenge-request","content":"Challenge request"},"276":{"id":"/legacy/api/providers-2","page_id":"/legacy/api/providers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/legacy/api/providers#challenge-response","content":"Challenge response"},"277":{"id":"/legacy/api/providers-3","page_id":"/legacy/api/providers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/legacy/api/providers#paid-request","content":"Paid request"},"278":{"id":"/legacy/api/providers-4","page_id":"/legacy/api/providers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/legacy/api/providers#success-response","content":"Success response"},"279":{"id":"/legacy/api/providers-5","page_id":"/legacy/api/providers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/legacy/api/providers#capability","content":"Capability"},"280":{"id":"/legacy/api/providers-6","page_id":"/legacy/api/providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/providers","content":"`HttpWebSearchProvider` (in `providers/web-search.ts`) talks to providers over plain HTTP. Any endpoint that implements this contract works with the router."},"281":{"id":"/legacy/api/providers-7","page_id":"/legacy/api/providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/providers#challenge-request","content":"The SDK sends the input as a JSON POST body:"},"282":{"id":"/legacy/api/providers-8","page_id":"/legacy/api/providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/providers#challenge-response","content":"A compliant provider replies HTTP 402 with a `payment-required` header containing a base64 (or base64url) encoded JSON `PaymentChallenge`:"},"283":{"id":"/legacy/api/providers-9","page_id":"/legacy/api/providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/providers#challenge-response","content":"A non-402 status, a missing header, or malformed base64 JSON raises `InvalidPaymentChallengeError` for that provider."},"284":{"id":"/legacy/api/providers-10","page_id":"/legacy/api/providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/providers#paid-request","content":"After settlement the SDK retries the same POST with the signed payload:"},"285":{"id":"/legacy/api/providers-11","page_id":"/legacy/api/providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/providers#success-response","content":"HTTP 200 with a JSON body of normalized shape:"},"286":{"id":"/legacy/api/providers-12","page_id":"/legacy/api/providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/providers#success-response","content":"`normalize` requires `results` to be an array whose items each have string `title`, `url`, and `snippet`. Anything else raises `ProviderResponseError`. A non-2xx response raises `ProviderExecutionError`."},"287":{"id":"/legacy/api/providers-13","page_id":"/legacy/api/providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/providers#capability","content":"The `Capability` type is `\"web.search\"`. Providers are matched to requests by exact capability string before being probed."},"288":{"id":"/legacy/api/utilities","page_id":"/legacy/api/utilities","type":"page","content":"Utilities","breadcrumbs":["EcoRouter Docs","Legacy SDK","API Reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/legacy/api/utilities"},"289":{"id":"/legacy/api/utilities-0","page_id":"/legacy/api/utilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/utilities","content":"Money parsing and provider selection helpers exported by the SDK."},"290":{"id":"/legacy/api/utilities-1","page_id":"/legacy/api/utilities","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/legacy/api/utilities#parseusdc","content":"parseUsdc"},"291":{"id":"/legacy/api/utilities-2","page_id":"/legacy/api/utilities","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/legacy/api/utilities#formatusdc","content":"formatUsdc"},"292":{"id":"/legacy/api/utilities-3","page_id":"/legacy/api/utilities","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/legacy/api/utilities#selectprovider","content":"selectProvider"},"293":{"id":"/legacy/api/utilities-4","page_id":"/legacy/api/utilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/utilities#parseusdc","content":"Parses a non-negative decimal string with at most 7 places into atomic units (USDC has 7 decimals, so `1` equals `10_000_000` atomic). Throws `TypeError` on any other input format."},"294":{"id":"/legacy/api/utilities-5","page_id":"/legacy/api/utilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/utilities#formatusdc","content":"Formats atomic units back to a decimal string, trimming trailing zeros. Throws `RangeError` for negative values."},"295":{"id":"/legacy/api/utilities-6","page_id":"/legacy/api/utilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/utilities#selectprovider","content":"Scores each candidate as `economicCost = priceAtomic / (qualityScore * successRate)` and returns the lowest. Ties break on lower `priceAtomic`, then lexically smaller `providerId`. Throws `RangeError` on an empty list. The result adds `economicCost` to the input fields."},"296":{"id":"/legacy/api/utilities-7","page_id":"/legacy/api/utilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/utilities#selectprovider","content":"All three are exported from the package root, so `import { selectProvider } from \"ecorouter\"` works."},"297":{"id":"/legacy/api/x402","page_id":"/legacy/api/x402","type":"page","content":"x402 Validation","breadcrumbs":["EcoRouter Docs","Legacy SDK","API Reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/legacy/api/x402"},"298":{"id":"/legacy/api/x402-0","page_id":"/legacy/api/x402","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/x402","content":"What validateChallenge checks, in order."},"299":{"id":"/legacy/api/x402-1","page_id":"/legacy/api/x402","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/legacy/api/x402#paymentchallenge","content":"PaymentChallenge"},"300":{"id":"/legacy/api/x402-2","page_id":"/legacy/api/x402","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/x402","content":"`validateChallenge(challenge, mandate, maxSpend, executionId?)` returns the accepted amount in atomic units, or throws. It runs these checks in exact order, from `x402/validate.ts`:"},"301":{"id":"/legacy/api/x402-3","page_id":"/legacy/api/x402","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/x402","content":"**Supported requirements.** `x402Version === 2`, `scheme === \"exact\"`, `network === \"stellar:testnet\"`, `asset === mandate.asset`, and a non-empty `payTo` string. Failure: `InvalidPaymentChallengeError`."},"302":{"id":"/legacy/api/x402-4","page_id":"/legacy/api/x402","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/x402","content":"**Amount format.** `amount` is a string matching `^\\d+$`. Failure: `InvalidPaymentChallengeError`."},"303":{"id":"/legacy/api/x402-5","page_id":"/legacy/api/x402","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/x402","content":"**Positive amount.** `BigInt(amount) > 0`. Failure: `InvalidPaymentChallengeError`."},"304":{"id":"/legacy/api/x402-6","page_id":"/legacy/api/x402","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/x402","content":"**Mandate not revoked.** `mandate.revoked` is false. Failure: `MandateRevokedError`."},"305":{"id":"/legacy/api/x402-7","page_id":"/legacy/api/x402","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/x402","content":"**Mandate not expired.** `mandate.expiresAt` is greater than the current Unix time in seconds. Failure: `MandateExpiredError`."},"306":{"id":"/legacy/api/x402-8","page_id":"/legacy/api/x402","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/x402","content":"**Local policy.** `amount <= parseUsdc(maxSpend)`. Failure: `PolicyExceededError`."},"307":{"id":"/legacy/api/x402-9","page_id":"/legacy/api/x402","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/x402","content":"**Mandate limits.** `amount <= mandate.maxPaymentAtomic` and `amount <= mandate.remainingAtomic`. Failure: `MandateExceededError`."},"308":{"id":"/legacy/api/x402-10","page_id":"/legacy/api/x402","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/x402","content":"Note the ordering consequences: a revoked or expired mandate throws before any policy check, and the local `maxSpend` cap is evaluated before the on-chain mandate caps."},"309":{"id":"/legacy/api/x402-11","page_id":"/legacy/api/x402","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/x402","content":"Inside `router.execute`, validation failures do not throw. They silently disqualify that provider; a provider is only removed from the eligible set."},"310":{"id":"/legacy/api/x402-12","page_id":"/legacy/api/x402","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/api/x402#paymentchallenge","content":"<TypeTable type=\"{ x402Version: { description: 'Must be 2.', type: 'number', required: true }, scheme: { description:…\" />"},"311":{"id":"/legacy/contract","page_id":"/legacy/contract","type":"page","content":"ecorouter-account contract","breadcrumbs":["EcoRouter Docs","Legacy SDK"],"tags":[],"url":"/legacy/contract"},"312":{"id":"/legacy/contract-0","page_id":"/legacy/contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/contract","content":"The single-agent Soroban smart account used by the legacy SDK."},"313":{"id":"/legacy/contract-1","page_id":"/legacy/contract","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/legacy/contract#the-mandate","content":"The Mandate"},"314":{"id":"/legacy/contract-2","page_id":"/legacy/contract","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/legacy/contract#public-functions","content":"Public functions"},"315":{"id":"/legacy/contract-3","page_id":"/legacy/contract","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/legacy/contract#what-__check_auth-enforces","content":"What `__check_auth` enforces"},"316":{"id":"/legacy/contract-4","page_id":"/legacy/contract","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/legacy/contract#errors","content":"Errors"},"317":{"id":"/legacy/contract-5","page_id":"/legacy/contract","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/legacy/contract#building-and-deploying","content":"Building and deploying"},"318":{"id":"/legacy/contract-6","page_id":"/legacy/contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/contract","content":"`contracts/ecorouter-account` is a `no_std` Soroban smart account (crate type `cdylib`). It holds funds, stores a spending mandate, and authorizes outbound transfers through the `__check_auth` custom account interface. All types and behaviors below come from `contracts/ecorouter-account/src/lib.rs`."},"319":{"id":"/legacy/contract-7","page_id":"/legacy/contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/contract#the-mandate","content":"A single mandate is stored in instance storage under `DataKey::Mandate`; the owner address is stored under `DataKey::Owner`."},"320":{"id":"/legacy/contract-8","page_id":"/legacy/contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/contract#public-functions","content":"| Function            | Auth                   | Effect                                                             |\n| ------------------- | ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `initialize(owner)` | `owner.require_auth()` | Stores the owner. Fails with `AlreadyInitialized` if called twice. |","table":"table-0"},"321":{"id":"/legacy/contract-9","page_id":"/legacy/contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/contract#public-functions","content":"| Function                                                                          | Auth  | Effect                                                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n| --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `create_mandate(session_public_key, asset, total_limit, max_payment, expires_at)` | owner | Creates the mandate with `spent = 0`, `revoked = false`. Rejects non-positive limits, `max_payment > total_limit` (`InvalidAmount`), and `expires_at` in the past (`InvalidExpiration`). Emits a `mandate created` event. |","table":"table-0"},"322":{"id":"/legacy/contract-10","page_id":"/legacy/contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/contract#public-functions","content":"| Function           | Auth  | Effect                                                  |\n| ------------------ | ----- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `revoke_mandate()` | owner | Sets `revoked = true`. Emits a `mandate revoked` event. |","table":"table-0"},"323":{"id":"/legacy/contract-11","page_id":"/legacy/contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/contract#public-functions","content":"| Function                      | Auth  | Effect                                                                                                                                                        |\n| ----------------------------- | ----- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `withdraw(asset, to, amount)` | owner | Transfers any token out of the contract via the token client. `amount` must be positive. This is the owner escape hatch; the session key can never invoke it. |","table":"table-0"},"324":{"id":"/legacy/contract-12","page_id":"/legacy/contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/contract#public-functions","content":"| Function        | Auth | Effect                                             |\n| --------------- | ---- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `get_mandate()` | none | Returns the current mandate, or `MandateNotFound`. |","table":"table-0"},"325":{"id":"/legacy/contract-13","page_id":"/legacy/contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/contract#public-functions","content":"| Function                                                    | Auth        | Effect                                                                                         |\n| ----------------------------------------------------------- | ----------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `__check_auth(signature_payload, signature, auth_contexts)` | session key | The authorization hook invoked by the Soroban host when the account is required as an invoker. |","table":"table-0"},"326":{"id":"/legacy/contract-14","page_id":"/legacy/contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/contract#what-__check_auth-enforces","content":"When a session key signs an invocation that requires this account's auth, the contract checks, in order:"},"327":{"id":"/legacy/contract-15","page_id":"/legacy/contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/contract#what-__check_auth-enforces","content":"A mandate exists (`MandateNotFound`), is not revoked (`MandateRevoked`), and has not expired (`MandateExpired`)."},"328":{"id":"/legacy/contract-16","page_id":"/legacy/contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/contract#what-__check_auth-enforces","content":"The signer public key equals `mandate.session_public_key` (`WrongSigner`), and the Ed25519 signature verifies over the payload."},"329":{"id":"/legacy/contract-17","page_id":"/legacy/contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/contract#what-__check_auth-enforces","content":"Exactly one authorization context, and it must be a `Context::Contract` call (`UnsupportedInvocation`). Administrative functions are structurally impossible for the session key."},"330":{"id":"/legacy/contract-18","page_id":"/legacy/contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/contract#what-__check_auth-enforces","content":"The called contract equals `mandate.asset` (`WrongAsset`), the function is `transfer` with exactly 3 arguments (`UnsupportedInvocation`)."},"331":{"id":"/legacy/contract-19","page_id":"/legacy/contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/contract#what-__check_auth-enforces","content":"The transfer source is the account contract itself (`WrongSource`) and `amount > 0` (`InvalidAmount`)."},"332":{"id":"/legacy/contract-20","page_id":"/legacy/contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/contract#what-__check_auth-enforces","content":"`amount <= mandate.max_payment` (`PaymentAboveMaximum`)."},"333":{"id":"/legacy/contract-21","page_id":"/legacy/contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/contract#what-__check_auth-enforces","content":"`spent + amount <= mandate.total_limit` (`AllowanceExceeded`), using checked arithmetic."},"334":{"id":"/legacy/contract-22","page_id":"/legacy/contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/contract#what-__check_auth-enforces","content":"On success the contract increments `spent` and emits a `payment authorized` event carrying asset, recipient, amount, new spent, and remaining allowance."},"335":{"id":"/legacy/contract-23","page_id":"/legacy/contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/contract#errors","content":"`AccountError`: `AlreadyInitialized` (1), `NotInitialized` (2), `InvalidAmount` (3), `InvalidExpiration` (4), `MandateNotFound` (5), `MandateRevoked` (6), `MandateExpired` (7), `WrongSigner` (8), `UnsupportedInvocation` (9), `WrongAsset` (10), `WrongSource` (11), `PaymentAboveMaximum` (12), `AllowanceExceeded` (13)."},"336":{"id":"/legacy/contract-24","page_id":"/legacy/contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/contract#building-and-deploying","content":"The contract is a standard Soroban `cdylib` crate. Build and deploy with the Stellar CLI (`stellar contract build`, `stellar contract deploy`), then call `initialize` with the owner address and `create_mandate` to bind a session key, asset, and limits. The repository does not ship deploy scripts; see the Soroban docs for network-specific commands."},"337":{"id":"/legacy/how-it-works","page_id":"/legacy/how-it-works","type":"page","content":"SDK pipeline","breadcrumbs":["EcoRouter Docs","Legacy SDK"],"tags":[],"url":"/legacy/how-it-works"},"338":{"id":"/legacy/how-it-works-0","page_id":"/legacy/how-it-works","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/how-it-works","content":"The execution pipeline inside router.execute in the legacy SDK."},"339":{"id":"/legacy/how-it-works-1","page_id":"/legacy/how-it-works","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/legacy/how-it-works#idempotency-check","content":"Idempotency check"},"340":{"id":"/legacy/how-it-works-2","page_id":"/legacy/how-it-works","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/legacy/how-it-works#load-the-mandate","content":"Load the mandate"},"341":{"id":"/legacy/how-it-works-3","page_id":"/legacy/how-it-works","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/legacy/how-it-works#filter-and-challenge-providers","content":"Filter and challenge providers"},"342":{"id":"/legacy/how-it-works-4","page_id":"/legacy/how-it-works","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/legacy/how-it-works#quality-filter-and-challenge-validation","content":"Quality filter and challenge validation"},"343":{"id":"/legacy/how-it-works-5","page_id":"/legacy/how-it-works","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/legacy/how-it-works#score-and-select","content":"Score and select"},"344":{"id":"/legacy/how-it-works-6","page_id":"/legacy/how-it-works","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/legacy/how-it-works#authorize-and-settle","content":"Authorize and settle"},"345":{"id":"/legacy/how-it-works-7","page_id":"/legacy/how-it-works","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/legacy/how-it-works#paid-execute-and-normalize","content":"Paid execute and normalize"},"346":{"id":"/legacy/how-it-works-8","page_id":"/legacy/how-it-works","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/legacy/how-it-works#return","content":"Return"},"347":{"id":"/legacy/how-it-works-9","page_id":"/legacy/how-it-works","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/how-it-works","content":"Every call to `router.execute` runs the same deterministic pipeline, implemented in `packages/sdk/src/ecorouter.ts`."},"348":{"id":"/legacy/how-it-works-10","page_id":"/legacy/how-it-works","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/how-it-works#idempotency-check","content":"The router resolves `executionId` (or generates a random UUID), then checks its in-memory execution map. A `complete` entry returns the cached result immediately. A `running`, `failed`, or `settlement_unknown` entry throws. Otherwise the id is marked `running`."},"349":{"id":"/legacy/how-it-works-11","page_id":"/legacy/how-it-works","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/how-it-works#load-the-mandate","content":"`paymentClient.loadMandate(account)` fetches the current on-chain `MandateState`: asset, `maxPaymentAtomic`, `remainingAtomic`, `expiresAt`, `revoked`."},"350":{"id":"/legacy/how-it-works-12","page_id":"/legacy/how-it-works","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/how-it-works#filter-and-challenge-providers","content":"Providers whose `capability` does not match the request are dropped. Every remaining provider gets a concurrent probe: `POST` the JSON input, expect HTTP 402 plus a `payment-required` header. Each challenge is raced against a 5000 ms timeout via `Promise.allSettled`, so one slow or broken provider cannot stall the rest."},"351":{"id":"/legacy/how-it-works-13","page_id":"/legacy/how-it-works","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/how-it-works#quality-filter-and-challenge-validation","content":"Providers below `policy.minimumQuality` are discarded. Each surviving challenge is checked by `validateChallenge` against the mandate and `policy.maxSpendUsdc`. Failures are discarded, not thrown. See x402 validation for the exact check order."},"352":{"id":"/legacy/how-it-works-14","page_id":"/legacy/how-it-works","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/how-it-works#score-and-select","content":"For each eligible offer the router reads the in-memory success metrics for that provider id. `successRate` is `successCount / total`, or `1` when there is no history. `selectProvider` computes `economicCost = priceAtomic / (qualityScore * successRate)` and picks the lowest, breaking ties on lower `priceAtomic`, then lexically smaller `providerId`. No eligible provider means `NoEligibleProviderError`."},"353":{"id":"/legacy/how-it-works-15","page_id":"/legacy/how-it-works","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/how-it-works#authorize-and-settle","content":"`paymentClient.authorizeAndSettle` signs the winning challenge with the session secret against the Soroban account. `PaymentAuthorizationError` and `PaymentSettlementError` propagate unchanged (the execution is marked `failed`). Any other exception marks the execution `settlement_unknown` and throws `PaymentSettlementUnknownError`, because the transfer may have gone through."},"354":{"id":"/legacy/how-it-works-16","page_id":"/legacy/how-it-works","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/how-it-works#paid-execute-and-normalize","content":"The provider is retried with the `payment-signature` header. The response must be `{ results: [{ title, url, snippet }] }`; anything else raises `ProviderResponseError`. Other failures raise `ProviderExecutionError` and count against the provider's metrics."},"355":{"id":"/legacy/how-it-works-17","page_id":"/legacy/how-it-works","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/how-it-works#return","content":"On success the provider's `successCount` increments and the router returns `EcoRouterExecutionResult`: the execution id, normalized output, the decision record (provider, price in USDC, quality, success rate, economic cost), the payment receipt, and the remaining mandate balance."},"356":{"id":"/legacy/how-it-works-18","page_id":"/legacy/how-it-works","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/how-it-works#return","content":"All token amounts are atomic integers (USDC has 7 decimals), never floating point. `maxSpendUsdc` strings are parsed by `parseUsdc`."},"357":{"id":"/legacy","page_id":"/legacy","type":"page","content":"SDK overview","breadcrumbs":["EcoRouter Docs","Legacy SDK"],"tags":[],"url":"/legacy"},"358":{"id":"/legacy-0","page_id":"/legacy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy","content":"The original EcoRouter TypeScript SDK for capability routing over x402. Kept for reference."},"359":{"id":"/legacy-1","page_id":"/legacy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy","content":"This section documents the original EcoRouter SDK. EcoRouter is now a product: a shared USDC spending account for teams and their AI agents. Start with the introduction for the current product. The SDK pages are kept for reference and are not where new work happens."},"360":{"id":"/legacy-2","page_id":"/legacy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy","content":"EcoRouter is a local TypeScript SDK for capability-based purchasing by autonomous agents. Instead of hardcoding an API vendor, your agent asks for a capability such as `web.search`. The SDK probes configured providers over HTTP 402 (x402 V2 `exact`), validates each offer against your local spend policy and the on-chain Soroban mandate, picks the best value deterministically, settles the payment in USDC on `stellar:testnet`, and normalizes the response into one predictable shape."},"361":{"id":"/legacy-3","page_id":"/legacy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy","content":"Everything runs on your machine. There are no hosted services, no registries, and no custodial wallets. Payment authorization is enforced on Stellar by the `ecorouter-account` Soroban smart account, which gates every transfer through `__check_auth` against a mandate you control."},"362":{"id":"/legacy-4","page_id":"/legacy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy","content":"<Card title=\"Quickstart\" href=\"/legacy/quickstart\" description=\"Install the SDK and run your first paid execution.\" />"},"363":{"id":"/legacy-5","page_id":"/legacy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy","content":"<Card title=\"How It Works\" href=\"/legacy/how-it-works\" description=\"The exact pipeline from probe to normalized result.\" />"},"364":{"id":"/legacy-6","page_id":"/legacy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy","content":"<Card title=\"Smart Account Contract\" href=\"/legacy/contract\" description=\"The Soroban mandate and what __check_auth enforces.\" />"},"365":{"id":"/legacy-7","page_id":"/legacy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy","content":"<Card title=\"API Reference\" href=\"/legacy/api/ecorouter\" description=\"Every interface, function, and error in the SDK.\" />"},"366":{"id":"/legacy-8","page_id":"/legacy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy","content":"<Card title=\"Playground\" href=\"/legacy/playground\" description=\"Run the real validation and selection functions in your browser.\" />"},"367":{"id":"/legacy/playground","page_id":"/legacy/playground","type":"page","content":"SDK playground","breadcrumbs":["EcoRouter Docs","Legacy SDK"],"tags":[],"url":"/legacy/playground"},"368":{"id":"/legacy/playground-0","page_id":"/legacy/playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/playground","content":"Run the legacy SDK validation and selection functions in your browser."},"369":{"id":"/legacy/playground-1","page_id":"/legacy/playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/playground","content":"These panels import the actual functions from `packages/sdk/src` (`validateChallenge`, `selectProvider`, `parseUsdc`, `formatUsdc`) and run them locally in your browser on every change. No network calls and no payments happen; nothing is signed or sent anywhere."},"370":{"id":"/legacy/quickstart","page_id":"/legacy/quickstart","type":"page","content":"SDK quickstart","breadcrumbs":["EcoRouter Docs","Legacy SDK"],"tags":[],"url":"/legacy/quickstart"},"371":{"id":"/legacy/quickstart-0","page_id":"/legacy/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/quickstart","content":"Install the legacy EcoRouter SDK and run your first execution."},"372":{"id":"/legacy/quickstart-1","page_id":"/legacy/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/legacy/quickstart#install","content":"Install"},"373":{"id":"/legacy/quickstart-2","page_id":"/legacy/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/legacy/quickstart#prerequisites","content":"Prerequisites"},"374":{"id":"/legacy/quickstart-3","page_id":"/legacy/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/legacy/quickstart#configure-the-router","content":"Configure the router"},"375":{"id":"/legacy/quickstart-4","page_id":"/legacy/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/legacy/quickstart#execute","content":"Execute"},"376":{"id":"/legacy/quickstart-5","page_id":"/legacy/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/legacy/quickstart#call-routerexecute","content":"Call `router.execute`"},"377":{"id":"/legacy/quickstart-6","page_id":"/legacy/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/legacy/quickstart#read-the-result","content":"Read the result"},"378":{"id":"/legacy/quickstart-7","page_id":"/legacy/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/quickstart#prerequisites","content":"You need three things before the router can pay for anything:"},"379":{"id":"/legacy/quickstart-8","page_id":"/legacy/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/quickstart#prerequisites","content":"**A deployed `ecorouter-account` Soroban contract** holding USDC on `stellar:testnet`, with an active mandate created via `create_mandate` (see Contract)."},"380":{"id":"/legacy/quickstart-9","page_id":"/legacy/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/quickstart#prerequisites","content":"**A session keypair** whose public key is the mandate's `session_public_key`."},"381":{"id":"/legacy/quickstart-10","page_id":"/legacy/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/quickstart#prerequisites","content":"**A `PaymentClient` implementation.** The SDK defines the interface but does not ship a concrete client. You supply the code that reads mandate state and submits the authorized transfer (see Payment Client)."},"382":{"id":"/legacy/quickstart-11","page_id":"/legacy/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/quickstart#configure-the-router","content":"The constructor validates the config: at least two providers, unique ids, HTTPS endpoints on public hostnames, and `qualityScore` between 0 and 1."},"383":{"id":"/legacy/quickstart-12","page_id":"/legacy/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/quickstart#read-the-result","content":"Reusing an `executionId` is safe: a completed execution returns its cached result. An id that is running, failed, or whose settlement state is unknown throws."},"384":{"id":"/legacy/quickstart-13","page_id":"/legacy/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/legacy/quickstart#read-the-result","content":"Want to see the internals live? Try the Playground, or read How It Works."},"385":{"id":"/quickstart","page_id":"/quickstart","type":"page","content":"Quickstart","breadcrumbs":["EcoRouter Docs"],"tags":[],"url":"/quickstart"},"386":{"id":"/quickstart-0","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart","content":"Run a team in the sandbox with no wallet, then do the same on Stellar testnet with Freighter."},"387":{"id":"/quickstart-1","page_id":"/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/quickstart#part-1-the-sandbox","content":"Part 1: the sandbox"},"388":{"id":"/quickstart-2","page_id":"/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/quickstart#open-the-sandbox","content":"Open the sandbox"},"389":{"id":"/quickstart-3","page_id":"/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/quickstart#read-the-rules","content":"Read the rules"},"390":{"id":"/quickstart-4","page_id":"/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/quickstart#pay-inside-the-rules","content":"Pay inside the rules"},"391":{"id":"/quickstart-5","page_id":"/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/quickstart#go-over-a-limit","content":"Go over a limit"},"392":{"id":"/quickstart-6","page_id":"/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/quickstart#approve-then-settle","content":"Approve, then settle"},"393":{"id":"/quickstart-7","page_id":"/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/quickstart#try-the-assistant","content":"Try the assistant"},"394":{"id":"/quickstart-8","page_id":"/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/quickstart#watch-the-agents","content":"Watch the agents"},"395":{"id":"/quickstart-9","page_id":"/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/quickstart#part-2-stellar-testnet-with-freighter","content":"Part 2: Stellar testnet with Freighter"},"396":{"id":"/quickstart-10","page_id":"/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/quickstart#deploy-the-contracts","content":"Deploy the contracts"},"397":{"id":"/quickstart-11","page_id":"/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/quickstart#fund-the-account","content":"Fund the account"},"398":{"id":"/quickstart-12","page_id":"/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/quickstart#connect-freighter","content":"Connect Freighter"},"399":{"id":"/quickstart-13","page_id":"/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/quickstart#add-spenders-and-pay","content":"Add spenders and pay"},"400":{"id":"/quickstart-14","page_id":"/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/quickstart#next","content":"Next"},"401":{"id":"/quickstart-15","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart","content":"The app lives at ecorouter.xyz/app. It offers two ways in: **Sandbox**, which runs entirely in your browser with test dollars, and **Stellar testnet**, which uses the real contracts and a Freighter wallet."},"402":{"id":"/quickstart-16","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart","content":"Testnet only, not audited. Never send real funds to an EcoRouter contract."},"403":{"id":"/quickstart-17","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#part-1-the-sandbox","content":"The sandbox needs no wallet and no install. It runs the same rules as the contract, in the same order, using a TypeScript mirror that is tested case for case against the contract's tests. Nothing you do there touches a network, and it stays in your browser until you reset it."},"404":{"id":"/quickstart-18","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#open-the-sandbox","content":"Go to /app/ and choose **Open the sandbox**. You get a team account called Northwind Labs, funded with $5,000 in test dollars. You are **Ada**, the owner. The team also has **Marcus**, a person, and two AI agents, **Scout** and **Atlas**, each with its own policy. A payment from Marcus is already waiting for your decision."},"405":{"id":"/quickstart-19","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#read-the-rules","content":"Open **Spenders**. Marcus has $1,000 a month, $250 per payment, 20 payments a month, and four services on his list: inference credits, web search, market data and `translate`. Nobody registered `translate`, so the registry will refuse it. Use **Add spender** to add someone of your own."},"406":{"id":"/quickstart-20","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#pay-inside-the-rules","content":"In the sidebar, switch **Signed in as** to Marcus. Open **New payment**, pick *Inference credits* and enter `120`. Before you submit, the right-hand panel runs every check in order with the arithmetic, for example `$180.00 + $120.00 = $300.00 of $1,000.00`. Pay, and a receipt appears in **Activity**."},"407":{"id":"/quickstart-21","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#go-over-a-limit","content":"Enter `420` instead. The cap is $250, so the panel shows **Over the per-payment cap, $170.00 over**, and the checks after it are not reached. Submit it anyway: the payment is **held**, and nothing moves. Choose **Ask the owner to approve it**."},"408":{"id":"/quickstart-22","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#approve-then-settle","content":"Switch back to Ada and open **Approvals**. Each request shows the spender, service, amount, the rule that caught it and how far over it was. **Approve** moves no money. **Settle payment** is a separate step that pays the service, as long as its payee has not changed since the request was filed."},"409":{"id":"/quickstart-23","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#try-the-assistant","content":"As Marcus, open **Assistant** and try the examples. `Top up our inference credits by $120` passes all five stages. `Pay Acme Labs $50 for consulting` is refused by the schema, because the assistant has no way to name a service that is not on the list. `$35 of translation…` passes the schema but the registry refuses it. `Pay $420 for inference…` is held by the policy."},"410":{"id":"/quickstart-24","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#watch-the-agents","content":"Open **Agents**. Scout buys $4 of web search every day; Atlas buys $12 of storage every week. Press **Run now**, or use **Settings → +1 day** to move the sandbox clock forward. One of Atlas's earlier payments was over its cap: it was refused and stopped there, because agents cannot ask for approval."},"411":{"id":"/quickstart-25","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#part-2-stellar-testnet-with-freighter","content":"On testnet the money is test USDC held by the `team-account` contract, services resolve through the `service-registry` contract, and every payment links to a transaction on the Stellar explorer."},"412":{"id":"/quickstart-26","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#deploy-the-contracts","content":"You need the Stellar CLI and Rust with the `wasm32v1-none` target. From the repository root:"},"413":{"id":"/quickstart-27","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#deploy-the-contracts","content":"The script creates and funds an `owner` identity, deploys the registry and a team account owned by it, registers five demo services, and writes the contract ids to `packages/app/.env.local`."},"414":{"id":"/quickstart-28","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#fund-the-account","content":"Get testnet USDC (for example from Circle's testnet faucet) and send it to the team-account contract address. There is no deposit function; the contract simply holds what is sent to it, and only the owner can withdraw."},"415":{"id":"/quickstart-29","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#connect-freighter","content":"Install Freighter, switch it to **Testnet**, and import the owner key (or propose a new owner with `propose_owner`). Run `pnpm dev:app`, choose **Connect Freighter**, and approve the connection. Every action is a transaction you sign in Freighter."},"416":{"id":"/quickstart-30","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#add-spenders-and-pay","content":"Add people by their own `G…` address; each signs their own payments from their own Freighter. For an agent, generate a key, add its address as an *AI agent* spender, and run the worker where the agent lives:"},"417":{"id":"/quickstart-31","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#add-spenders-and-pay","content":"The agent's account needs a little XLM for fees."},"418":{"id":"/quickstart-32","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#next","content":"Spenders and policies for every rule a policy can hold."},"419":{"id":"/quickstart-33","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#next","content":"Approvals for how held payments are handled."},"420":{"id":"/quickstart-34","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#next","content":"Security model for the exact check order and the current limits."},"421":{"id":"/security","page_id":"/security","type":"page","content":"Security model","breadcrumbs":["EcoRouter Docs"],"tags":[],"url":"/security"},"422":{"id":"/security-0","page_id":"/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security","content":"What the contract checks, in what order, and what is not done yet."},"423":{"id":"/security-1","page_id":"/security","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/security#the-principle","content":"The principle"},"424":{"id":"/security-2","page_id":"/security","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/security#check-order-in-pay","content":"Check order in `pay`"},"425":{"id":"/security-3","page_id":"/security","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/security#settling-an-approved-exception","content":"Settling an approved exception"},"426":{"id":"/security-4","page_id":"/security","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/security#assistant-pipeline","content":"Assistant pipeline"},"427":{"id":"/security-5","page_id":"/security","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/security#what-is-not-done","content":"What is not done"},"428":{"id":"/security-6","page_id":"/security","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/security#reporting-a-problem","content":"Reporting a problem"},"429":{"id":"/security-7","page_id":"/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security","content":"EcoRouter is on **Stellar testnet only** and the contracts are **not audited**. Use test funds. Do not rely on it to protect real money."},"430":{"id":"/security-8","page_id":"/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security#the-principle","content":"**The agent proposes. Only the contract authorizes.** The app, the assistant and agents all pre-check payments so you see problems early, but those checks are a convenience. The rules that decide whether money moves are in the `team-account` contract, which holds the funds and runs every check itself."},"431":{"id":"/security-9","page_id":"/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security#check-order-in-pay","content":"`pay(spender, service, amount, memo, key)` runs these checks in this order. The first one that fails stops the call and nothing is transferred."},"432":{"id":"/security-10","page_id":"/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security#check-order-in-pay","content":"| #   | Check          | Fails when                         | Error           | Can a person ask for approval? |\n| --- | -------------- | ---------------------------------- | --------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| 1   | Account paused | The owner paused the team account. | `AccountPaused` | No                             |","table":"table-0"},"433":{"id":"/security-11","page_id":"/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security#check-order-in-pay","content":"| #   | Check          | Fails when                   | Error            | Can a person ask for approval? |\n| --- | -------------- | ---------------------------- | ---------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| 2   | Spender exists | The caller is not a spender. | `UnknownSpender` | No                             |","table":"table-0"},"434":{"id":"/security-12","page_id":"/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security#check-order-in-pay","content":"| #   | Check          | Fails when                     | Error           | Can a person ask for approval? |\n| --- | -------------- | ------------------------------ | --------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| 3   | Spender paused | The owner paused this spender. | `SpenderPaused` | No                             |","table":"table-0"},"435":{"id":"/security-13","page_id":"/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security#check-order-in-pay","content":"| #   | Check          | Fails when                      | Error           | Can a person ask for approval? |\n| --- | -------------- | ------------------------------- | --------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| 4   | Policy expired | The policy's expiry has passed. | `PolicyExpired` | No                             |","table":"table-0"},"436":{"id":"/security-14","page_id":"/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security#check-order-in-pay","content":"| #   | Check      | Fails when                      | Error           | Can a person ask for approval? |\n| --- | ---------- | ------------------------------- | --------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| 5   | Amount > 0 | The amount is zero or negative. | `InvalidAmount` | No                             |","table":"table-0"},"437":{"id":"/security-15","page_id":"/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security#check-order-in-pay","content":"| #   | Check                | Fails when                                    | Error               | Can a person ask for approval? |\n| --- | -------------------- | --------------------------------------------- | ------------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| 6   | Service on allowlist | The service id is not on this spender's list. | `ServiceNotAllowed` | Yes                            |","table":"table-0"},"438":{"id":"/security-16","page_id":"/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security#check-order-in-pay","content":"| #   | Check             | Fails when                 | Error              | Can a person ask for approval? |\n| --- | ----------------- | -------------------------- | ------------------ | ------------------------------ |\n| 7   | Replay key unused | This key was already used. | `DuplicatePayment` | No                             |","table":"table-0"},"439":{"id":"/security-17","page_id":"/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security#check-order-in-pay","content":"| #   | Check           | Fails when                         | Error            | Can a person ask for approval? |\n| --- | --------------- | ---------------------------------- | ---------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| 8   | Per-payment cap | The amount is above `max_payment`. | `OverPaymentCap` | Yes                            |","table":"table-0"},"440":{"id":"/security-18","page_id":"/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security#check-order-in-pay","content":"| #   | Check               | Fails when                                           | Error           | Can a person ask for approval? |\n| --- | ------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- | --------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| 9   | Payments per period | The spender already made `max_payments` this period. | `OverFrequency` | Yes                            |","table":"table-0"},"441":{"id":"/security-19","page_id":"/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security#check-order-in-pay","content":"| #   | Check          | Fails when                                    | Error           | Can a person ask for approval? |\n| --- | -------------- | --------------------------------------------- | --------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| 10  | Allowance left | The amount is above what is left this period. | `OverAllowance` | Yes                            |","table":"table-0"},"442":{"id":"/security-20","page_id":"/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security#check-order-in-pay","content":"| #   | Check             | Fails when                                      | Error                                | Can a person ask for approval? |\n| --- | ----------------- | ----------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------ | ------------------------------ |\n| 11  | Registry resolves | The id is unknown or suspended in the registry. | `UnknownService`, `ServiceSuspended` | No                             |","table":"table-0"},"443":{"id":"/security-21","page_id":"/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security#check-order-in-pay","content":"| #   | Check             | Fails when                              | Error               | Can a person ask for approval? |\n| --- | ----------------- | --------------------------------------- | ------------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| 12  | Balance covers it | The account holds less than the amount. | `InsufficientFunds` | No                             |","table":"table-0"},"444":{"id":"/security-22","page_id":"/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security#check-order-in-pay","content":"| #   | Check              | Fails when                                                     | Error | Can a person ask for approval? |\n| --- | ------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------- | ----- | ------------------------------ |\n| 13  | Transfer + receipt | USDC moves to the resolved payee and a `pay` event is emitted. |       |                                |","table":"table-0"},"445":{"id":"/security-23","page_id":"/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security#check-order-in-pay","content":"When a check fails, the call fails and nothing moves. If the failing rule is one of the four marked \"Yes\", the app shows the payment as **held** and a person can file an approval request for it. An agent cannot file requests (`AgentCannotRequest`), so for an agent every failure is a refusal. The contract's `check` function runs the same rules as a dry run, which is how the app shows the arithmetic before you sign."},"446":{"id":"/security-24","page_id":"/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security#check-order-in-pay","content":"The spender must also authorize the call with its own Stellar signature, so no one can pay on another spender's behalf."},"447":{"id":"/security-25","page_id":"/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security#settling-an-approved-exception","content":"Approving a request and moving money are separate transactions. `settle` refuses if the account is paused, the request is not approved or has expired (requests last 7 days), the service no longer resolves, or the balance is too low, and it **refuses if the service's payee changed** since the request was filed. An approval covers one payment, to one payee, for one amount. Settled exceptions do not count against the spender's allowance."},"448":{"id":"/security-26","page_id":"/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security#assistant-pipeline","content":"Requests typed in plain words pass through five stages before reaching `pay`: sentence, assistant, schema, registry, policy. The output schema has no address field, so an invented recipient cannot be expressed. See Assistant."},"449":{"id":"/security-27","page_id":"/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security#what-is-not-done","content":"Be clear about the current limits:"},"450":{"id":"/security-28","page_id":"/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security#what-is-not-done","content":"**Not audited.** No third party has reviewed the contracts or the app."},"451":{"id":"/security-29","page_id":"/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security#what-is-not-done","content":"**Testnet only.** There is no mainnet deployment. Test USDC only."},"452":{"id":"/security-30","page_id":"/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security#what-is-not-done","content":"**The registry owner controls the registry.** It registers services and can suspend them. A suspended service stops receiving payments from every team that uses it until it is resumed. Teams trust the registry owner for this."},"453":{"id":"/security-31","page_id":"/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security#what-is-not-done","content":"**A payee can rotate its payout address.** Ordinary payments after a rotation go to the new address. Approved exceptions are protected: settlement refuses if the payee changed after the request, but in-policy payments are not held for a payee change."},"454":{"id":"/security-32","page_id":"/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security#what-is-not-done","content":"**Agent keys are hot keys.** An agent's key lives wherever the agent runs. The policy bounds the damage, so keep agent policies tight."},"455":{"id":"/security-33","page_id":"/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security#what-is-not-done","content":"**The sandbox is a mirror.** It runs a TypeScript copy of the contract's rules for demos. It is not a security boundary, and the contract is the source of truth if they ever differ."},"456":{"id":"/security-34","page_id":"/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security#reporting-a-problem","content":"Open an issue on GitHub. For anything sensitive, ask for a private contact in the issue rather than posting details."}},"count":456},"sorting":{"language":"multilingual","sortableProperties":["content","page_i