37,"199":428,"200":227,"201":74,"202":188,"203":231,"204":12,"205":4,"206":23,"207":14,"208":15,"209":76,"210":78,"211":77,"212":75,"213":297,"214":61,"215":65,"216":64,"217":62,"218":57,"219":55,"220":226,"221":404,"222":233,"223":322,"224":220,"225":252,"226":234,"227":67,"228":37,"229":71,"230":43,"231":33,"232":426,"233":189,"234":159,"235":69,"236":70,"237":38,"238":238,"239":244,"240":317,"241":178,"242":98,"243":94,"244":100,"245":99,"246":101,"247":102,"248":92,"249":95,"250":93,"251":96,"252":97,"253":205,"254":72,"255":253,"256":312,"257":400,"258":314,"259":282,"260":362,"261":236,"262":408,"263":66,"264":39,"265":68,"266":51,"267":50,"268":423,"269":46,"270":49,"271":208,"272":8,"273":323,"274":396,"275":213,"276":214,"277":303,"278":369,"279":212,"280":42,"281":409,"282":160,"283":162,"284":174,"285":265,"286":44,"287":379,"288":430,"289":283,"290":305,"291":257,"292":355,"293":304,"294":256,"295":346,"296":179,"297":453,"298":444,"299":313,"300":53,"301":27,"302":7,"303":24,"304":19,"305":18,"306":16,"307":17,"308":285,"309":272,"310":73,"311":232,"312":412,"313":397,"314":326,"315":435,"316":239,"317":210,"318":41,"319":167,"320":126,"321":105,"322":127,"323":113,"324":128,"325":106,"326":447,"327":161,"328":411,"329":250,"330":389,"331":415,"332":36,"333":52,"334":290,"335":34,"336":392,"337":348,"338":393,"339":266,"340":280,"341":254,"342":328,"343":345,"344":200,"345":302,"346":338,"347":243,"348":405,"349":48,"350":325,"351":324,"352":255,"353":47,"354":402,"355":291,"356":180,"357":347,"358":398,"359":422,"360":228,"361":249,"362":60,"363":58,"364":63,"365":56,"366":59,"367":349,"368":343,"369":419,"370":350,"371":275,"372":273,"373":321,"374":217,"375":251,"376":211,"377":330,"378":455,"379":1,"380":3,"381":0,"382":391,"383":339,"384":432,"385":329,"386":341,"387":306,"388":298,"389":331,"390":311,"391":261,"392":194,"393":425,"394":434,"395":307,"396":222,"397":258,"398":218,"399":172,"400":284,"401":384,"402":374,"403":406,"404":262,"405":295,"406":271,"407":235,"408":371,"409":196,"410":294,"411":292,"412":454,"413":407,"414":260,"415":274,"416":171,"417":382,"418":368,"419":192,"420":352,"421":351,"422":443,"423":401,"424":216,"425":361,"426":199,"427":441,"428":336,"429":230,"430":29,"431":45,"432":87,"433":90,"434":89,"435":88,"436":91,"437":79,"438":84,"439":85,"440":80,"441":86,"442":82,"443":83,"444":81,"445":445,"446":413,"447":195,"448":337,"449":203,"450":20,"451":28,"452":30,"453":2,"454":6,"455":31,"456":296},"orderedDocs":[[381,"**A `PaymentClient` implementation.** The SDK defines the interface but does not ship a concrete client. You supply the code that reads mandate state and submits the authorized transfer (see Payment Client)."],[379,"**A deployed `ecorouter-account` Soroban contract** holding USDC on `stellar:testnet`, with an active mandate created via `create_mandate` (see Contract)."],[453,"**A payee can rotate its payout address.** Ordinary payments after a rotation go to the new address. Approved exceptions are protected: settlement refuses if the payee changed after the request, but in-policy payments are not held for a payee change."],[380,"**A session keypair** whose public key is the mandate's `session_public_key`."],[205,"**Add spenders.** Each person or agent gets a policy. The owner can pause or remove a spender at any time."],[104,"**Add** a spender with an address and a policy."],[454,"**Agent keys are hot keys.** An agent's key lives wherever the agent runs. The policy bounds the damage, so keep agent policies tight."],[302,"**Amount format.** `amount` is a string matching `^\\d+$`. Failure: `InvalidPaymentChallengeError`."],[272,"**Any other thrown value marks the execution `settlement_unknown`** and the router throws `PaymentSettlementUnknownError`, because the payment may have succeeded. A `settlement_unknown` execution id cannot be retried; retrying throws. Only throw a generic error when settlement truly is ambiguous."],[28,"**Approve or decline.** The owner decides. Declining closes the request and writes a declined receipt."],[27,"**Ask for approval.** The spender files a request (`request_approval`). It lands on the owner's **Approvals** screen with the spender, service, amount, memo, the rule that caught it and the overage. The contract also records the service's payee at that moment. Requests expire after 7 days."],[105,"**Edit** the policy at any time. Changes apply to the next payment; the current period and its usage are kept."],[204,"**Fund one account.** The owner deposits USDC into the team account contract."],[26,"**Held.** The spender sees which rule caught the payment and how far over it was, for example `per-payment cap $250 · over by $70`."],[207,"**Hold what breaks a rule.** A payment over a limit is held, not failed. Nothing moves until the owner approves and the payment is settled in a separate step."],[208,"**Keep a receipt for everything.** Settled, held, declined and refused payments all show up in Activity, with a link to the Stellar transaction when one exists."],[306,"**Local policy.** `amount <= parseUsdc(maxSpend)`. Failure: `PolicyExceededError`."],[307,"**Mandate limits.** `amount <= mandate.maxPaymentAtomic` and `amount <= mandate.remainingAtomic`. Failure: `MandateExceededError`."],[305,"**Mandate not expired.** `mandate.expiresAt` is greater than the current Unix time in seconds. Failure: `MandateExpiredError`."],[304,"**Mandate not revoked.** `mandate.revoked` is false. Failure: `MandateRevokedError`."],[450,"**Not audited.** No third party has reviewed the contracts or the app."],[106,"**Pause** a spender to stop them immediately without losing their history. **Resume** to undo."],[8,"**Pay on a schedule.** For example, `$5 every day` to a `market-data` service."],[206,"**Pay registered services.** Payments go to services in the on-chain service registry, named by id, never by address."],[303,"**Positive amount.** `BigInt(amount) > 0`. Failure: `InvalidPaymentChallengeError`."],[107,"**Remove** a spender to delete their policy. Their address can no longer pay; past receipts stay."],[29,"**Settle.** Approving does not move money. Settlement (`settle`) is its own transaction, sent by the owner or by the spender who asked. It refuses if the service's payee changed since the request was filed, and also if the account is paused, the request expired, the service is now unknown or suspended, or the balance is too low. A settled exception does not count against the spender's allowance."],[301,"**Supported requirements.** `x402Version === 2`, `scheme === \"exact\"`, `network === \"stellar:testnet\"`, `asset === mandate.asset`, and a non-empty `payTo` string. Failure: `InvalidPaymentChallengeError`."],[451,"**Testnet only.** There is no mainnet deployment. Test USDC only."],[430,"**The agent proposes. Only the contract authorizes.** The app, the assistant and agents all pre-check payments so you see problems early, but those checks are a convenience. The rules that decide whether money moves are in the `team-account` contract, which holds the funds and runs every check itself."],[452,"**The registry owner controls the registry.** It registers services and can suspend them. A suspended service stops receiving payments from every team that uses it until it is resumed. Teams trust the registry owner for this."],[455,"**The sandbox is a mirror.** It runs a TypeScript copy of the contract's rules for demos. It is not a security boundary, and the contract is the source of truth if they ever differ."],[147,"`__constructor(owner, asset, registry)` sets the owner, the token contract to pay in (USDC) and the service registry. The account starts unpaused with no spenders."],[231,"`account` or `sessionSecret` is empty, or fewer than two providers are given."],[335,"`AccountError`: `AlreadyInitialized` (1), `NotInitialized` (2), `InvalidAmount` (3), `InvalidExpiration` (4), `MandateNotFound` (5), `MandateRevoked` (6), `MandateExpired` (7), `WrongSigner` (8), `UnsupportedInvocation` (9), `WrongAsset` (10), `WrongSource` (11), `PaymentAboveMaximum` (12), `AllowanceExceeded` (13)."],[183,"`AccountPaused` (1), `UnknownSpender` (2), `SpenderPaused` (3), `PolicyExpired` (4), `InvalidAmount` (5), `ServiceNotAllowed` (6), `DuplicatePayment` (7), `OverPaymentCap` (8), `OverFrequency` (9), `OverAllowance` (10), `UnknownService` (11), `ServiceSuspended` (12), `InsufficientFunds` (13), `InvalidPolicy` (14), `UnknownRequest` (15), `RequestNotPending` (16), `RequestNotApproved` (17), `RequestExpired` (18), `PayeeChanged` (19), `NotAuthorized` (20), `NoExceptionNeeded` (21), `NotEligibleForException` (22), `AgentCannotRequest` (23), `RegistryUnavailable` (24), `NoPendingOwner` (25)."],[332,"`amount <= mandate.max_payment` (`PaymentAboveMaximum`)."],[228,"`ArbiterConfig` is an alias of `EcoRouterConfig`, and `Arbiter` is an alias of the `EcoRouter` class."],[237,"`ArbiterExecutionResult` is an alias of `EcoRouterExecutionResult`."],[264,"`authorizeAndSettle` receives `{ account, sessionSecret, executionId, providerId, challenge }`."],[175,"`check(spender, service, amount) -> Verdict` runs the same rules without auth or state changes and returns `{ rule, over_by, allowance_left, period_spent, period_count }`. `rule` is `0` when the payment would go through, otherwise the error code that would refuse it. The app uses this to show the arithmetic before anything is signed."],[318,"`contracts/ecorouter-account` is a `no_std` Soroban smart account (crate type `cdylib`). It holds funds, stores a spending mandate, and authorizes outbound transfers through the `__check_auth` custom account interface. All types and behaviors below come from `contracts/ecorouter-account/src/lib.rs`."],[280,"`HttpWebSearchProvider` (in `providers/web-search.ts`) talks to providers over plain HTTP. Any endpoint that implements this contract works with the router."],[230,"`new EcoRouter(config)` throws `TypeError` when:"],[286,"`normalize` requires `results` to be an array whose items each have string `title`, `url`, and `snippet`. Anything else raises `ProviderResponseError`. A non-2xx response raises `ProviderExecutionError`."],[431,"`pay(spender, service, amount, memo, key)` runs these checks in this order. The first one that fails stops the call and nothing is transferred."],[269,"`PaymentAuthorizationError` when signing or authorization definitively failed."],[353,"`paymentClient.authorizeAndSettle` signs the winning challenge with the session secret against the Soroban account. `PaymentAuthorizationError` and `PaymentSettlementError` propagate unchanged (the execution is marked `failed`). Any other exception marks the execution `settlement_unknown` and throws `PaymentSettlementUnknownError`, because the transfer may have gone through."],[349,"`paymentClient.loadMandate(account)` fetches the current on-chain `MandateState`: asset, `maxPaymentAtomic`, `remainingAtomic`, `expiresAt`, `revoked`."],[270,"`PaymentSettlementError` when the transfer definitively failed on-chain."],[267,"`SettlementReceipt` is `{ transactionHash: string }`. The hash is returned in `result.payment.transactionHash`."],[266,"`SignedPayment` is `{ payload: string; transactionHash?: string }`. The payload is sent back to the provider in the `payment-signature` header."],[333,"`spent + amount <= mandate.total_limit` (`AllowanceExceeded`), using checked arithmetic."],[300,"`validateChallenge(challenge, mandate, maxSpend, executionId?)` returns the accepted amount in atomic units, or throws. It runs these checks in exact order, from `x402/validate.ts`:"],[176,"`version()`, `owner()`, `asset()`, `registry()`, `paused()`, `balance()`, `spenders()`, `policy(spender) -> Option<Policy>`, `usage(spender) -> Usage`, `request(id) -> Option<ApprovalRequest>`, `requests(from, limit)`, `is_key_used(spender, key)`."],[219,"<Card title=\"Agents\" href=\"/concepts/agents\" description=\"Give an AI agent its own key and policy.\" />"],[365,"<Card title=\"API Reference\" href=\"/legacy/api/ecorouter\" description=\"Every interface, function, and error in the SDK.\" />"],[218,"<Card title=\"Contracts reference\" href=\"/contracts\" description=\"Functions on team-account and service-registry.\" />"],[363,"<Card title=\"How It Works\" href=\"/legacy/how-it-works\" description=\"The exact pipeline from probe to normalized result.\" />"],[366,"<Card title=\"Playground\" href=\"/legacy/playground\" description=\"Run the real validation and selection functions in your browser.\" />"],[362,"<Card title=\"Quickstart\" href=\"/legacy/quickstart\" description=\"Install the SDK and run your first paid execution.\" />"],[214,"<Card title=\"Quickstart\" href=\"/quickstart\" description=\"Run a team in the sandbox, then on Stellar testnet with Freighter.\" />"],[217,"<Card title=\"Security model\" href=\"/security\" description=\"The exact check order, and what is not done yet.\" />"],[364,"<Card title=\"Smart Account Contract\" href=\"/legacy/contract\" description=\"The Soroban mandate and what __check_auth enforces.\" />"],[216,"<Card title=\"Spenders and policies\" href=\"/concepts/spenders\" description=\"Allowance, cap, payment count, expiry and approved services.\" />"],[215,"<Card title=\"Team account\" href=\"/concepts/team-account\" description=\"The shared account, its owner and its balance.\" />"],[263,"<TypeTable type=\"{ 'loadMandate(account)': { description: 'Read the current on-chain mandate for the account contract…\" />"],[227,"<TypeTable type=\"{ account: { description: 'Address of the deployed ecorouter-account contract. Required, non-empty.'…\" />"],[265,"<TypeTable type=\"{ asset: { description: 'Asset identifier the mandate allows (USDC).', type: 'string', required: tru…\" />"],[235,"<TypeTable type=\"{ executionId: { description: 'Idempotency key. A random UUID is generated when omitted.', type: 'st…\" />"],[236,"<TypeTable type=\"{ executionId: { description: 'The idempotency key used for this run.', type: 'string', required: tr…\" />"