                                                                 |\n| -------------------- | --------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `settle(id, caller)` | owner or the spender who filed it | Pays an approved request. Refuses if the account is paused, the request is not approved or has expired, the service no longer resolves, **the payee changed since the request was filed** (`PayeeChanged`), or the balance is too low. Settled exceptions do not consume the spender's allowance. |"],[153,"| Function             | Effect                                                                                                               |\n| -------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `set_paused(paused)` | Pauses or resumes the whole account. A paused account authorizes nothing, including settlement of approved requests. |"],[320,"| Function            | Auth                   | Effect                                                             |\n| ------------------- | ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `initialize(owner)` | `owner.require_auth()` | Stores the owner. Fails with `AlreadyInitialized` if called twice. |"],[322,"| Function           | Auth  | Effect                                                  |\n| ------------------ | ----- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `revoke_mandate()` | owner | Sets `revoked = true`. Emits a `mandate revoked` event. |"],[324,"| Function        | Auth | Effect                                             |\n| --------------- | ---- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `get_mandate()` | none | Returns the current mandate, or `MandateNotFound`. |"],[155,"| Function      | Effect                                                 |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `approve(id)` | Approves a pending, unexpired request. Moves no money. |"],[156,"| Function      | Effect                                                |\n| ------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `decline(id)` | Declines a pending or approved-but-unsettled request. |"],[62,"| Outcome      | Meaning                                 | Money moved |\n| ------------ | --------------------------------------- | ----------- |\n| **Declined** | The owner declined an approval request. | No          |"],[63,"| Outcome     | Meaning                                                          | Money moved |\n| ----------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------- |\n| **Refused** | A check that cannot be approved failed, or an agent hit a limit. | No          |"],[60,"| Outcome     | Meaning                                                  | Money moved |\n| ----------- | -------------------------------------------------------- | ----------- |\n| **Settled** | Every check passed and USDC went to the service's payee. | Yes         |"],[61,"| Outcome  | Meaning                                                        | Money moved |\n| -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------- |\n| **Held** | A limit caught the payment. It may become an approval request. | No          |"],[97,"| Rule                    | Field          | Example | What it does                                          |\n| ----------------------- | -------------- | ------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| Max payments per period | `max_payments` | 20      | How many payments the spender may make in one period. |"],[94,"| Rule                 | Field       | Example | What it does                             |\n| -------------------- | ----------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| Allowance per period | `allowance` | $1,000  | Total the spender may pay in one period. |"],[99,"| Rule              | Field      | Example                           | What it does                                          |\n| ----------------- | ---------- | --------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| Approved services | `services` | `inference-credits`, `gpu-rental` | The only service ids this spender may pay (up to 32). |"],[96,"| Rule            | Field         | Example | What it does                                                    |\n| --------------- | ------------- | ------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Cap per payment | `max_payment` | $250    | No single payment may be larger. Must not exceed the allowance. |"],[98,"| Rule   | Field        | Example    | What it does                                            |\n| ------ | ------------ | ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Expiry | `expires_at` | 2026-12-31 | After this time, the policy stops authorizing anything. |"],[95,"| Rule   | Field    | Example | What it does                                                                           |\n| ------ | -------- | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Period | `period` | 30 days | Length of a period. Periods are fixed windows counted from when the spender was added. |"],[100,"| Rule   | Field    | Example | What it does                              |\n| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| Paused | `paused` | false   | When true, the spender cannot pay at all. |"],[93,"| Rule  | Field   | Example | What it does    |\n| ----- 