-------------------------------------------------- |\n| 5. Policy | The full contract policy runs. | A rule fails. A person's limit becomes a hold; anything else is refused. |"],[77,"| State              | Effect on payment                           |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------- |\n| Registered, active | Resolves to its payee. Payment can proceed. |"],[78,"| State      | Effect on payment                         |\n| ---------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| Unknown id | Resolution fails and the payment reverts. |"],[79,"| State     | Effect on payment                                                      |\n| --------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Suspended | Resolution fails and the payment reverts until the service is resumed. |"],[181,"| Topics                                          | Emitted by            |\n| ----------------------------------------------- | --------------------- |\n| `policy`, `set` / `paused` / `removed`, spender | owner spender changes |"],[182,"| Topics                           | Emitted by               |\n| -------------------------------- | ------------------------ |\n| `account`, `paused` / `withdraw` | `set_paused`, `withdraw` |"],[179,"| Topics                   | Emitted by           |\n| ------------------------ | -------------------- |\n| `request`, `decided`, id | `approve`, `decline` |"],[180,"| Topics                   | Emitted by |\n| ------------------------ | ---------- |\n| `request`, `settled`, id | `settle`   |"],[177,"| Topics                  | Emitted by                                                  |\n| ----------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `pay`, spender, service | `pay` (the receipt: payee, amount, memo, key, period_spent) |"],[178,"| Topics                 | Emitted by         |\n| ---------------------- | ------------------ |\n| `request`, `filed`, id | `request_approval` |"],[91,"A **spender** is a Stellar address that may pay from the team account: a teammate's wallet or an AI agent's key. Each spender has exactly one **policy**, set by the owner."],[234,"A `qualityScore` is outside 0 to 1."],[282,"A compliant provider replies HTTP 402 with a `payment-required` header containing a base64 (or base64url) encoded JSON `PaymentChallenge`:"],[327,"A mandate exists (`MandateNotFound`), is not revoked (`MandateRevoked`), and has not expired (`MandateExpired`)."],[283,"A non-402 status, a missing header, or malformed base64 JSON raises `InvalidPaymentChallengeError` for that provider."],[66,"A payment that fails a check never reaches the chain as a transfer, so held, declined and refused receipts are kept by the app; requests and decisions are also recorded as contract events."],[11,"A person who hits a limit can ask for approval. An agent cannot: its policy's `kind` is `Agent`, and the contract answers `request_approval` with `AgentCannotRequest`. Its refused payments end with a refused receipt and nothing moves. This keeps an agent from filling the owner's Approvals screen, and it makes the policy the single place where an agent's room to spend is decided."],[102,"A policy only ever narrows what a spender can do. There is no rule that lets a spender pay an address directly, and no rule that lets one spender use another's allowance."],[81,"A service's **payee** can **rotate its payout address**, for example to move to a new wallet."],[319,"A single mandate is stored in instance storage under `DataKey::Mandate`; the owner address is stored under `DataKey::Owner`."],[83,"A spender's policy lists the service ids it may pay. The contract checks the allowlist before it checks the registry, so a payment to a registered service that is not on a spender's list fails for that spender. A person can ask the owner for a one-off approval; an agent cannot."],[115,"A team account is one instance of the `team-account` contract on Stellar. It holds the team's USDC and a policy for every spender. Nobody holds the money directly: not the owner's wallet, not a teammate, not an agent's key. Money leaves the account only through the contract's own functions, after its checks pass."],[161,"Account paused → `AccountPaused`"],[416,"Add people by their own `G…` address; each signs their own payments from their own Freighter. For an agent, generate a key, add its address as an *AI agent* spender, and run the worker where the agent lives:"],[399,"Add spenders and pay"],[118,"add, change, pause, resume and remove spenders,"],[284,"After settlement the SDK retries the same POST with the signed payload:"],[1,"Agents"],[24,"Agents do not ask"],[149,"All of these require the owner's signature."],[241,"All SDK errors extend `EcoRouterError` (alias `ArbiterError`), which carries `code: EcoRouterErrorCode` and an optional `executionId`."],[296,"All three are exported from the package root, so `import { selectProvider } from \"ecorouter\"` works."],[356,"All token amounts are atomic integers (USDC has 7 decimals), never floating point. `maxSpendUsdc` strings are parsed by `parseUsdc`."],[170,"Allowance left this period → `OverAllowance`"],[165,"Amount > 0 → `InvalidAmount`"],[53,"Amounts are read from the sentence by deterministic code and compared with what the model returns. The model cannot change the amount you typed. If the sentence is ambiguous, the request stops at stage 1 and asks you to be specific."],[125,"Amounts are USDC in 7-decimal integer units on chain. The app shows dollars and cents, and its pre-check uses the same integer arithmetic as the contract."],[7,"An **agent** is a spender that is a program rather than a person. It is added to the team account like any other spender, with two differences: it signs with its own Stellar key, and its payments that break a rule are refused instead of held."],[39,"An agent's payment that breaks a limit is refused and stops there. It does not create an approval request. If an agent needs more room, the owner changes its policy. See Agents."],[2,"An AI agent is a spender with its own Stellar key and its own policy."],[202,"An assistant or an agent can suggest a payment, and the app can pre-check it, but neither can move money on its own. The only thing that moves money is the `team-account` contract, and it runs the same checks on every payment, in the same order."],[233,"An endpoint is not HTTPS, or its hostname is local (localhost, private ranges, link-local, IPv6 ULA)."],[122,"Anyone can fund the account: it is an ordinary USDC transfer to the contract's address. The app's **Deposit** action does exactly that."],[20,"Approvals"],[419,"Approvals for how held payments are handled."],[120,"approve or decline approval requests,"],[392,"Approve, then settle"],[447,"Approving a request and moving money are separate transactions. `settle` refuses if the account is paused, the request is not approved or has expired (requests last 7 days), the service no longer resolves, or the balance is too low, and it **refuses if the service's payee changed** since the request was filed. An approval covers one payment, to one payee, for one amount. Settled exceptions do not count against the spender's allowance."],[409,"As Marcus, open **Assistant** and try the examples. `Top up our inference credits by $120` passes all five stages. `Pay Acme Labs $50 for consulting` is refused by the schema, because the assistant has no way to name a service that is not on the list. `$35 of translation…` passes the schema but the registry refuses it. `Pay $420 for inference…` is held by the policy."],[41,"Ask for a payment in plain words. Five stages check it, and any one can refuse."],[40,"Assistant"],[426,"Assistant pipeline"],[344,"Authorize and settle"],[112,"Balance and spend"],[172,"Balance covers the amount → `InsufficientFunds`"],[449,"Be clear about the current limits:"],[82,"Because the payee can change, an approved exception records the payee at the time of the request, and settlement refuses if the payee has changed since. The owner then has to look at the request again."],[253,"Beyond `code` and `executionId`, it carries:"],[108,"Both are spenders and both go through the same checks. The difference is what happens after a payment breaks a limit: a person's payment is held and can become an approval request; an agent's payment is refused and stops there. The contract knows which is which from the policy's `kind`."],[195,"Both are standard Soroban crates. Build and deploy with the Stellar CLI (`stellar contract build`, `stellar contract deploy`) against testnet. Deploy the registry first, then the team account with the registry's address."],[271,"Both propagate unchanged and mark the execution `failed`, so the same `executionId` can be retried."],[142,"Building"],[317,"Building and deploying"],[376,"Call `router.execute`"],[279,"Capability"],[275,"Challenge request"],[276,"Challenge response"],[135,"Check order in `pay`"],[424,"Check order in `pay`"],[374,"Configure the router"],[398,"Connect Freighter"],[132,"Construction"],[224,"Constructor validation"],[129,"Contracts reference"],[396,"Deploy the contracts"],[136,"Dry run"],[10,"Each agent gets its own Stellar key. That key is only useful as that spender: it cannot withdraw, change policies, approve requests or pay services outside its list. If the key leaks, the most it can do is what the agent's policy already allows, and the owner can pause or remove the agent at once."],[116,"Each team account has one **owner**, the address that created it. Only the owner can:"],[220,"EcoRouter"],[200,"EcoRouter gives a team one shared USDC account on Stellar. Every spender on that account, whether a person or an AI agent, pays under its own on-chain policy: an allowance per period, a cap per payment, a maximum number of payments, an expiry date and a list of approved services. The policy is enforced by a Soroban contract that holds the money."],[360,"EcoRouter is a local TypeScript SDK for capability-based purchasing by autonomous agents. Instead of hardcoding an API vendor, your agent asks for a capability such as `web.search`. The SDK probes configured providers over HTTP 402 (x402 V2 `exact`), validates each offer against your local spend policy and the on-chain Soroban mandate, picks the best value deterministically, settles the payment in USDC on `stellar:testnet`, and normalizes the response into one predictable shape."],[197,"EcoRouter is a shared USDC spending account on Stellar for teams and their AI agents."],[429,"EcoRouter is on **Stellar testnet only** and the contracts are **not audited**. Use test funds. Do not rely on it to protect real money."],[203,"EcoRouter runs on **Stellar testnet only** and the contracts are **not audited**. Use test funds. The sandbox runs the same rules in your browser, using a TypeScript mirror of the contract, so you can try everything without a wallet."],[311,"ecorouter-account contract"],[222,"EcoRouterConfig"],[226,"EcoRouterExecutionResult"],[407,"Enter `420` instead. The cap is $250, so the panel shows **Over the per-payment cap, $170.00 over**, and the checks after it are not reached. Submit it anyway: the payment is **held**, and nothing moves. Choose **Ask the owner to approve it**."],[261,"Error contract"],[140,"Errors"],[238,"Errors"],[316,"Errors"],[194,"Errors: `NotInitialized` (1), `AlreadyRegistered` (2), `UnknownService` (3), `ServiceSuspended` (4), `NoPendingOwner` (5)."],[139,"Events"],[193,"Events: `service registered`, `service payee` (old and new payee), `service suspended`."],[347,"Every call to `router.execute` runs the same deterministic pipeline, implemented in `packages/sdk/src/ecorouter.ts`."],[239,"Every EcoRouterErrorCode, its class, and when it is thrown."],[101,"Every limit must be positive. A zero never means \"no limit\"."],[56,"Every payment attempt leaves a receipt in Activity."],[9,"Every payment goes through the full contract check order. The agent's policy decides how much, how often, until when and to which services."],[86,"Every person and every agent pays under its own on-chain policy."],[361,"Everything runs on your machine. There are no hosted services, no registries, and no custodial wallets. Payment authorization is enforced on Stellar by the `ecorouter-account` Soroban smart account, which gates every transfer through `__check_auth` against a mandate you control."],[329,"Exactly one authorization context, and it must be a `Context::Contract` call (`UnsupportedInvocation`). Administrative functions are structurally impossible for the session key."],[375,"Execute"],[225,"ExecuteRequest"],[255,"Executions that end `settlement_unknown` cannot be retried under the same `executionId`; the router throws instead of risking a double payment."],[341,"Filter and challenge providers"],[352,"For each eligible offer the router reads the in-memory success metrics for that provider id. `successRate` is `successCount / total`, or `1` when there is no history. `selectProvider` computes `economicCost = priceAtomic / (qualityScore * successRate)` and picks the lowest, breaking ties on lower `priceAtomic`, then lexically smaller `providerId`. No eligible provider means `NoEligibleProviderError`."],[294,"Formats atomic units back to a decimal string, trimming trailing zeros. Throws `RangeError` for negative values."],[291,"formatUsdc"],[397,"Fund the account"],[12,"Generate a Stellar key for the agent where it will run. The web app never holds it."],[414,"Get testnet USDC (for example from Circle's testnet faucet) and send it to the team-account contract address. There is no deposit function; the contract simply holds what is sent to it, and only the owner can withdraw."],[391,"Go over a limit"],[404,"Go to /app/ and choose **Open the sandbox**. You get a team account called Northwind Labs, funded with $5,000 in test dollars. You are **Ada**, the owner. The team also has **Marcus**, a person, and two AI agents, **Scout** and **Atlas**, each with its own policy. A payment from Marcus is already waiting for your decision."],[121,"hand ownership to another address (a two-step propose and accept)."],[64,"Held, declined and refused receipts carry the rule that stopped the payment and, for limits, how far over it was."],[285,"HTTP 200 with a JSON body of normalized shape:"],[339,"Idempotency check"],[123,"In the app, the owner sees the **Overview** (balance, spend this period, spenders) and the **Approvals** screen."],[67,"In the sandbox, receipts are kept in your browser."],[18,"In the sandbox, the browser tab plays the worker: schedules run on their own, and **Run now** runs one immediately."],[127,"In the sandbox, the team account is a TypeScript object in your browser that mirrors the contract's rules and check order. On testnet, it is a deployed `team-account` contract and every change is a signed transaction."],[406,"In the sidebar, switch **Signed in as** to Marcus. Open **New payment**, pick *Inference credits* and enter `120`. Before you submit, the right-hand panel runs every check in order with the arithmetic, for example `$180.00 + $120.00 = $300.00 of $1,000.00`. Pay, and a receipt appears in **Activity**."],[309,"Inside `router.execute`, validation failures do not throw. They silently disqualify that provider; a provider is only removed from the eligible set."],[372,"Install"],[415,"Install Freighter, switch it to **Testnet**, and import the owner key (or propose a new owner with `propose_owner`). Run `pnpm dev:app`, choose **Connect Freighter**, and approve the connection. Every action is a transaction you sign in Freighter."],[371,"Install the legacy EcoRouter SDK and run your first execution."],[196,"Introduction"],[54,"It cannot add services to a list, raise a cap, approve a request or pay an address. Those are owner actions or do not exist at all."],[4,"Its own key"],[30,"Keeping approval and settlement separate means an approval is a decision about one specific payment to one specific payee, not a blank cheque."],[340,"Load the mandate"],[89,"Managing spenders"],[259,"MandateState"],[289,"Money parsing and provider selection helpers exported by the SDK."],[400,"Next"],[308,"Note the ordering consequences: a revoked or expired mandate throws before any policy check, and the local `maxSpend` cap is evaluated before the on-chain mandate caps."],[14,"On **Agents**, record its schedule (amount, service, every hour/day/week) so the team can see what it is meant to do."],[13,"On **Spenders**, add the agent's address as an *AI agent* with a tight policy: a small cap, a low allowance, a short expiry and only the services it needs."],[58,"On chain"],[65,"On Stellar testnet, a settled payment emits a `pay` event from the `team-account` contract carrying the spender, service, payee, amount, memo and the spender's spend this period. Settled exceptions emit a `request settled` event. The receipt in the app links to the Stellar transaction so anyone can check it. The replay key passed to `pay` means the same payment cannot be settled twice, even if the app retries."],[334,"On success the contract increments `spent` and emits a `payment authorized` event carrying asset, recipient, amount, new spent, and remaining allowance."],[355,"On success the provider's `successCount` increments and the router returns `EcoRouterExecutionResult`: the execution id, normalized output, the decision record (provider, price in USDC, quality, success rate, economic cost), the payment receipt, and the remaining mandate balance."],[411,"On testnet the money is test USDC held by the `team-account` contract, services resolve through the `service-registry` contract, and every payment links to a transaction on the Stellar explorer."],[110,"One shared USDC account, held by a Soroban contract, that every spender pays from."],[410,"Open **Agents**. Scout buys $4 of web search every day; Atlas buys $12 of storage every week. Press **Run now**, or use **Settings → +1 day** to move the sandbox clock forward. One of Atlas's earlier payments was over its cap: it was refused and stopped there, because agents cannot ask for approval."],[405,"Open **Spenders**. Marcus has $1,000 a month, $250 per payment, 20 payments a month, and four services on his list: inference credits, web search, market data and `translate`. Nobody registered `translate`, so the registry will refuse it. Use **Add spender** to add someone of your own."],[456,"Open an issue on GitHub. For anything sensitive, ask for a private contact in the issue rather than posting details."],[213,"Open the app at ecorouter.xyz/app and pick one."],[388,"Open the sandbox"],[57,"Outcomes"],[21,"Over a limit, a payment is held, not failed, and the owner decides."],[133,"Owner functions"],[345,"Paid execute and normalize"],[277,"Paid request"],[293,"Parses a non-negative decimal string with at most 7 places into atomic units (USDC has 7 decimals, so `1` equals `10_000_000` atomic). Throws `TypeError` on any other input format."],[290,"parseUsdc"],[387,"Part 1: the sandbox"],[395,"Part 2: Stellar testnet with Freighter"],[119,"pause and unpause the whole account,"],[113,"Pausing the account"],[126,"Pausing the account stops every payment from every spender at the first check, before anything else is looked at. It also blocks settlement of approved requests. Deposits and owner actions still work. Unpause to resume."],[390,"Pay inside the rules"],[256,"Payment Client"],[299,"PaymentChallenge"],[258,"PaymentClient"],[69,"Payments go to registered services, named by id, never to a raw address."],[169,"Payments per period (`max_payments`) → `OverFrequency`"],[240,"PaymentSettlementUnknownError"],[90,"People and agents"],[168,"Per-payment cap (`max_payment`) → `OverPaymentCap`"],[164,"Policy expired → `PolicyExpired`"],[373,"Prerequisites"],[223,"ProviderConfig"],[273,"Providers"],[351,"Providers below `policy.minimumQuality` are discarded. Each surviving challenge is checked by `validateChallenge` against the mandate and `policy.maxSpendUsdc`. Failures are discarded, not thrown. See x402 validation for the exact check order."],[350,"Providers whose `capability` does not match the request are dropped. Every remaining provider gets a concurrent probe: `POST` the JSON input, expect HTTP 402 plus a `payment-required` header. Each challenge is raced against a 5000 ms timeout via `Promise.allSettled`, so one slow or broken provider cannot stall the rest."],[314,"Public functions"],[130,"Public functions, types, events and errors of the team-account and service-registry Soroban contracts."],[342,"Quality filter and challenge validation"],[385,"Quickstart"],[377,"Read the result"],[389,"Read the rules"],[55,"Receipts"],[5,"Refused means refused"],[171,"Registry resolves the service → `UnknownService`, `ServiceSuspended` or `RegistryUnavailable`"],[167,"Replay key unused → `DuplicatePayment`"],[428,"Reporting a problem"],[448,"Requests typed in plain words pass through five stages before reaching `pay`: sentence, assistant, schema, registry, policy. The output schema has no address field, so an invented recipient cannot be expressed. See Assistant."],[346,"Return"],[383,"Reusing an `executionId` is safe: a completed execution returns its cached result. An id that is running, failed, or whose settlement state is unknown throws."],[174,"Rules 6, 8, 9 and 10 are **exception-eligible**: a person whose payment fails one of them can call `request_approval`. Agents get `AgentCannotRequest`."],[386,"Run a team in the sandbox with no wallet, then do the same on Stellar testnet with Freighter."],[15,"Run the agent worker with its key:"],[368,"Run the legacy SDK validation and selection functions in your browser."],[114,"Sandbox vs testnet"],[343,"Score and select"],[295,"Scores each candidate as `economicCost = priceAtomic / (qualityScore * successRate)` and returns the lowest. Ties break on lower `priceAtomic`, then lexically smaller `providerId`. Throws `RangeError` on an empty list. The result adds `economicCost` to the input fields."],[357,"SDK overview"],[337,"SDK pipeline"],[367,"SDK playground"],[370,"SDK quickstart"],[421,"Security model"],[420,"Security model for the exact check order and the current limits."],[84,"See Contracts reference for the functions."],[128,"See Contracts reference for the functions."],[292,"selectProvider"],[166,"Service on the spender's allowlist → `ServiceNotAllowed`"],[68,"Service registry"],[141,"service-registry"],[73,"Services and spenders"],[6,"Setting one up"],[425,"Settling an approved exception"],[260,"SignedPayment and SettlementReceipt"],[31,"Some checks cannot be overridden by an approval:"],[162,"Spender exists → `UnknownSpender`"],[134,"Spender functions"],[163,"Spender paused → `SpenderPaused`"],[85,"Spenders and policies"],[418,"Spenders and policies for every rule a policy can hold."],[278,"Success response"],[19,"Suggested starting point for a data-feed agent: cap `$5`, allowance `$150 / month`, max payments `31 / month`, one approved service."],[408,"Switch back to Ada and open **Approvals**. Each request shows the spender, service, amount, the rule that caught it and how far over it was. **Approve** moves no money. **Settle payment** is a separate step that pays the service, as long as its payee has not changed since the request was filed."],[109,"Team account"],[131,"team-account"],[402,"Testnet only, not audited. Never send real funds to an EcoRouter contract."],[59,"The **Activity** screen lists every payment attempt as a receipt. A receipt records who paid (the spender), the service id, the amount, the memo, the time, and the outcome."],[46,"The **assistant** lets a spender type a sentence such as `top up our inference credits by $120` instead of filling in the payment form. What it produces is a **proposal**. It has no power to pay; the contract still decides."],[80,"The **registry owner** registers services and can **suspend** or **resume** them. Service ids are never reused."],[74,"The **service registry** is a separate contract, `service-registry`, that maps a service id such as `inference-credits` to the Stellar address that receives payment for it (the **payee**)."],[287,"The `Capability` type is `\"web.search\"`. Providers are matched to requests by exact capability string before being probed."],[37,"the account does not hold enough USDC."],[32,"the account or the spender is paused,"],[417,"The agent's account needs a little XLM for fees."],[34,"the amount is zero or negative,"],[401,"The app lives at ecorouter.xyz/app. It offers two ways in: **Sandbox**, which runs entirely in your browser with test dollars, and **Stellar testnet**, which uses the real contracts and a Freighter wallet."],[103,"The app shows the same arithmetic the contract runs. For a spender with an allowance of $900, $340 already spent and a cap of $250:"],[88,"The arithmetic"],[52,"The assistant's output shape has **no address field**. The only way to name a destination is a service id, and the only ids it may choose are on the spender's list. An invented address has nowhere to go, and an invented id fails at the registry."],[124,"The balance is the USDC the contract holds. \"Spent this period\" is the sum of what spenders have paid inside their current periods. Each spender's allowance is tracked separately, so one spender running out never blocks another."],[330,"The called contract equals `mandate.asset` (`WrongAsset`), the function is `transfer` with exactly 3 arguments (`UnsupportedInvocation`)."],[33,"the caller is not a spender, or the policy has expired,"],[382,"The constructor validates the config: at least two providers, unique ids, HTTPS endpoints on public hostnames, and `qualityScore` between 0 and 1."],[336,"The contract is a standard Soroban `cdylib` crate. Build and deploy with the Stellar CLI (`stellar contract build`, `stellar contract deploy`), then call `initialize` with the owner address and `create_mandate` to bind a session key, asset, and limits. The repository does not ship deploy scripts; see the Soroban docs for network-specific commands."],[338,"The execution pipeline inside router.execute in the legacy SDK."],[42,"The five stages"],[22,"The flow"],[274,"The HTTP contract a web.search provider must implement."],[313,"The Mandate"],[358,"The original EcoRouter TypeScript SDK for capability routing over x402. Kept for reference."],[111,"The owner"],[257,"The PaymentClient interface you implement, its types, and its error contract."],[423,"The principle"],[354,"The provider is retried with the `payment-signature` header. The response must be `{ results: [{ title, url, snippet }] }`; anything else raises `ProviderResponseError`. Other failures raise `ProviderExecutionError` and count against the provider's metrics."],[35,"the replay key was already used,"],[221,"The router class, its config, and the execution request and result types."],[348,"The router resolves `executionId` (or generates a random UUID), then checks its in-memory execution map. A `complete` entry returns the cached result immediately. A `running`, `failed`, or `settlement_unknown` entry throws. Otherwise the id is marked `running`."],[403,"The sandbox needs no wallet and no install. It runs the same rules as the contract, in the same order, using a TypeScript mirror that is tested case for case against the contract's tests. Nothing you do there touches a network, and it stays in your browser until you reset it."],[413,"The script creates and funds an `owner` identity, deploys the registry and a team account owned by it, registers five demo services, and writes the contract ids to `packages/app/.env.local`."],[262,"The SDK does not ship a Stellar transport implementation. You provide a `PaymentClient` that reads mandate state and submits the authorized transfer. The router treats its return value and its errors precisely."],[281,"The SDK sends the input as a JSON POST body:"],[36,"the service is unknown or suspended in the registry,"],[328,"The signer public key equals `mandate.session_public_key` (`WrongSigner`), and the Ed25519 signature verifies over the payload."],[312,"The single-agent Soroban smart account used by the legacy SDK."],[446,"The spender must also authorize the call with its own Stellar signature, so no one can pay on another spender's behalf."],[75,"The team account's `pay` function takes a service id. It has no parameter for a destination address. At the end of its checks the contract asks the registry to resolve the id, and pays whatever address the registry returns."],[331,"The transfer source is the account contract itself (`WrongSource`) and `amount > 0` (`InvalidAmount`)."],[16,"The worker records each payment's idempotency key before submitting. After a crash it asks the contract whether that key was used (`is_key_used`) rather than paying again."],[148,"There is no deposit function. To fund the account, transfer USDC to the contract's address; `balance()` reads the contract's token balance."],[38,"These are **refused** outright. Even a request for a service outside the spender's list must name a service the registry resolves; payments never go to a raw address."],[369,"These panels import the actual functions from `packages/sdk/src` (`validateChallenge`, `selectProvider`, `parseUsdc`, `formatUsdc`) and run them locally in your browser on every change. No network calls and no payments happen; nothing is signed or sent anywhere."],[146,"This page summarizes the public interface. The Rust source in `contracts/` is authoritative. Amounts are in the asset's atomic units (USDC has 7 decimals). Times are ledger timestamps in seconds."],[76,"This removes a whole class of mistakes and attacks: a mistyped address, a pasted address from a phishing message, or an address invented by a language model cannot be expressed as a payment."],[359,"This section documents the original EcoRouter SDK. EcoRouter is now a product: a shared USDC spending account for teams and their AI agents. Start with the introduction for the current product. The SDK pages are kept for reference and are not where new work happens."],[268,"Throw the typed errors for definite failures:"],[173,"Transfer, then the `pay` receipt event"],[393,"Try the assistant"],[232,"Two providers share the same `id`."],[143,"Two Soroban contracts make up EcoRouter on Stellar. Both live in the repository under `contracts/`."],[199,"Two ways in"],[138,"Types"],[288,"Utilities"],[137,"Views"],[384,"Want to see the internals live? Try the Playground, or read How It Works."],[17,"Watch its receipts in **Activity**."],[394,"Watch the agents"],[315,"What `__check_auth` enforces"],[87,"What a policy holds"],[198,"What a team does with it"],[3,"What an agent can do"],[71,"What can happen to a service"],[23,"What cannot be approved"],[427,"What is not done"],[45,"What the assistant cannot do"],[422,"What the contract checks, in what order, and what is not done yet."],[298,"What validateChallenge checks, in order."],[445,"When a check fails, the call fails and nothing moves. If the failing rule is one of the four marked \"Yes\", the app shows the payment as **held** and a person can file an approval request for it. An agent cannot file requests (`AgentCannotRequest`), so for an agent every failure is a refusal. The contract's `check` function runs the same rules as a dry run, which is how the app shows the arithmetic before you sign."],[25,"When a person's payment breaks one of four rules, it is **held**: the service is not on their approved list, the amount is over the cap per payment, they have used up their payments for the period, or the amount is over the allowance left. Nothing moves. The payment is not lost either: the spender can ask the owner for an exception to that one payment."],[326,"When a session key signs an invocation that requires this account's auth, the contract checks, in order:"],[72,"Who controls what"],[43,"Why a hallucinated recipient cannot happen"],[70,"Why payments take an id, not an address"],[44,"Why the amount comes from code"],[117,"withdraw funds,"],[297,"x402 Validation"],[412,"You need the Stellar CLI and Rust with the `wasm32v1-none` target. From the repository root:"],[378,"You need three things before the router can pay for anything:"]],"type":"string"},"page_id":{"docs":{"1":24,"2":25,"3":26,"4":27,"5":28,"6":29,"7":30,"8":31,"9":32,"10":33,"11":34,"12":35,"13":36,"14":37,"15":38,"16":39,"17":40,"18":41,"19":42,"20":43,"21":44,"22":45,"23":46,"24":47,"25":48,"26":49,"27":50,"28":51,"29":52,"30":53,"31":54,"32":55,"33":56,"34":57,"35":58,"36":59,"37":60,"38":61,"39":62,"40":63,"41":64,"42":65,"43":66,"44":67,"45":68,"46":69,"47":70,"48":71,"49":72,"50":73,"51":74,"52":75,"53":76,"54":77,"55":78,"56":79,"57":80,"58":81,"59":82,"60":83,"61":84,"62":85,"63":86,"64":87,"65":88,"66":89,"67":90,"68":91,"69":92,"70":93,"71":94,"72":95,"73":96,"74":97,"75":98,"76":99,"77":100,"78":101,"79":102,"80":103,"81":104,"82":105,"83":106,"84":107,"85":108,"86":109,"87":110,"88":111,"89":112,"90":113,"91":114,"92":115,"93":116,"94":117,"95":118,"96":119,"97":120,"98":121,"99":122,"100":123,"101":124,"102":125,"103":126,"104":127,"105":128,"106":129,"107":130,"108":131,"109":132,"110":133,"111":134,"112":135,"113":136,"114":137,"115":138,"116":139,"117":140,"118":141,"119":142,"120":143,"121":144,"122":145,"123":146,"124":147,"125":148,"126":149,"127":150,"128":151,"129":152,"130":153,"131":154,"132":155,"133":156,"134":157,"135":158,"136":159,"137":160,"138":161,"139":162,"140":163,"141":164,"142":165,"143":166,"144":167,"145":168,"146":169,"147":170,"148":171,"149":172,"150":173,"151":174,"152":175,"153":176,"154":177,"155":178,"156":179,"157":180,"158":181,"159":182,"160":183,"161":184,"162":185,"163":186,"164":187,"165":188,"166":189,"167":190,"168":191,"169":192,"170":193,"171":194,"172":195,"173":196,"174":197,"175":198,"176":199,"177":200,"178":201,"179":202,"180":203,"181":204,"182":205,"183":206,"184":207,"185":208,"186":209,"187"